{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HhpiVQnsxrPZ6JbeTFz8d1","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"d0f4b1bf5be04ad6f9c567635864b36de6ac36c3","date":"2026-10-07T13:20:03.000Z","author":"Veronica Mukuhi Muthee","subject":"(feat) O3-5823: Capture diagnosis rank and certainty in the visit note (#3621)","message":"(feat) O3-5823: Capture diagnosis rank and certainty in the visit note (#3621)","ticketKeys":["O3-5823"],"pullRequests":[3621],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","hash":"0e1edc234479890d45bc09e67b2ee25befc1c803","date":"2026-10-05T11:52:41.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-6027: Clear order and diagnosis submissions on every write (#826)","message":"(fix) O3-6027: Clear order and diagnosis submissions on every write (#826)\n\n* (fix) Clear order and diagnosis submissions on every write\n\nOrdersAdapter and EncounterDiagnosisAdapter now clear the field's\nsubmission at the start of transformFieldValue, the same way ObsAdapter\nalready does.\n\ngracefullySetSubmission only sets values and never clears them, so a\nnewValue from an earlier write stayed on the field after it was\ncleared. On a new encounter, selecting an order or diagnosis and then\nclearing the field still submitted it. On an edited encounter, swapping\na stored order or diagnosis for another value and then clearing the\nfield still submitted the swapped value: a NEW order alongside the\nvoid, or an edit of the stored diagnosis to the swapped concept.\nClearing first means nothing is submitted for a new encounter and only\nthe void goes out for an edited one.\n\neditOrder no longer needs its own clearSubmission call when the value\nmatches the stored order, since the submission is already empty.\n\n* Fixup","ticketKeys":["O3-6027"],"pullRequests":[826],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-bedmanagement","hash":"a6aa20a5afb9ee7b9fa2fd2eac251e36455b10d2","date":"2026-10-05T10:22:50.000Z","author":"Ken Omondi","subject":"BED-40: Ending a visit with no bed assignment must not require bed write privileges (#119)","message":"BED-40: Ending a visit with no bed assignment must not require bed write privileges (#119)\n\n* BED-40: ending a visit with no bed assignment must not require bed write privileges\n\nVisitWithBedPatientAssignmentSaveHandler called unAssignBedsInEndedVisit on\nevery save of an ended visit. That method requires \"Assign Beds\" and\n\"Edit Admission Locations\", so a user who may end visits but not manage beds\ngot an APIAuthenticationException even when the patient never had a bed.\n\nOnly call it when the visit has an active bed assignment. Ending a visit\nthat does hold a bed still requires both privileges.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PLmE4JrqYk2DTfmUfu4SqY\n\n* BED-40: merge the end-visit condition into one if statement\n\nSonarCloud flagged the nested if (java:S1066). The three conditions are now\none if, in the same short-circuit order, so the bed lookup still runs only\nfor a persisted, ended visit. Behaviour is unchanged; api 124, atom-feed 5\nand omod 41 tests pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PLmE4JrqYk2DTfmUfu4SqY\n\n* BED-40: wrap the comment so the formatter keeps it, and commit the formatted tests\n\nThe comment is wrapped as suggested in review, so the formatter that runs at\ncompile leaves it whole. The two test classes are committed as the formatter\nwrites them, so a build changes none of the three files.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[119],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","hash":"ebb02b719931d121419669b531b6e05c77f515e9","date":"2026-10-02T18:57:25.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-6030: Keep hidden obs group members, orders and diagnoses out of submissions (#822)","message":"(fix) O3-6030: Keep hidden obs group members, orders and diagnoses out of submissions (#822)\n\n* (fix) Keep hidden obs group members, orders and diagnoses out of submissions\n\nHide logic only kept hidden top-level obs out of the encounter payload.\nHidden obs group members, test orders and diagnoses kept whatever value\nwas entered before the field was hidden, so they were still submitted\neven though the form no longer showed them.\n\nprocessObsGroup now skips hidden members and, in edit mode, voids their\nstored obs, the same way top-level obs are handled. It reads each\nmember's visibility and stored obs from the flattened form field,\nbecause hide evaluation and hydration update that copy rather than the\none held in the group's questions. prepareOrders and prepareDiagnosis\nnow skip hidden fields.\n\n* Evaluate hide logic for repeated field instances\n\nRows added to a repeating field kept their hidden state from when they\nwere created, so hiding a repeating test order, diagnosis or obs group\nmember left its extra rows in the encounter payload. Extra group rows\nalso stayed visible in the form.\n\nfindFieldSection looks up the field's page through meta.pageId, which\nrepeated instances don't carry because cloneRepeatField replaces their\nmeta. Reading sections off the missing page threw inside the\nfieldDependents loop in handleFieldLogic, so none of the repeated\ninstances had their hide expression re-evaluated. It now returns\nundefined when the page isn't found, which skips the section visibility\nupdate for repeated instances since they aren't in the form schema.\n\n* (fix) Preserve pending deletions for hidden orders and diagnoses\n\nFiltering hidden fields out of encounter submissions discarded explicit deletions when a previously cleared field became hidden. Keep pending voided values for hidden orders and diagnoses while excluding their new values. Leave stored values untouched when no deletion is pending, and preserve existing submission behavior for visible fields.\n\n* Skip delete","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":["O3-6030"],"pullRequests":[822],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","hash":"f8aa79f6e3c0814d0f9bf8449fb79dbe08558dd0","date":"2026-10-02T17:36:05.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(feat) O3-5823: Add certainty display and blue/gray defaults to diagnosis tags (#1881)","message":"(feat) O3-5823: Add certainty display and blue/gray defaults to diagnosis tags (#1881)","ticketKeys":["O3-5823"],"pullRequests":[1881],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"a0834be003ea69917f36dac8b4bccba52ba8a7a4","date":"2026-10-02T05:50:44.000Z","author":"chibongho","subject":"(fix) O3-6020: Make Visit Notes workspace accept an Encounter object for editing (#3719)","message":"(fix) O3-6020: Make Visit Notes workspace accept an Encounter object for editing (#3719)\n\n* (fix) O3-6020: Make Visit Notes workspace accept a Encounter object for editing\n\n* address feedback\n\n---------","ticketKeys":["O3-6020"],"pullRequests":[3719],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"108c48985b5e33905d025cb936a5657f45bb7a7a","date":"2026-09-24T20:50:01.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5998: Continue to the requested workspace after starting or selecting a visit (#3688)","message":"(fix) O3-5998: Continue to the requested workspace after starting or selecting a visit (#3688)\n\n* (fix) O3-5998: Continue to the requested workspace after starting or selecting a visit\n\nWhen a chart action needs a visit and the patient has none,\nuseStartVisitIfNeeded shows a visit prompt and waits for the user to start\nor pick a visit. Neither path continued to the workspace the user asked\nfor, so they had to click the action again.\n\nWith RDE off, the start visit dialog passes onVisitStarted into the\nstart-visit-workspace-form workspace, but the chart's wrapper for that\nworkspace never read it, so the promise never resolved. The wrapper now\naccepts onVisitStarted and calls it after it sets the visit context.\n\nWith RDE on, selecting a visit resolved the promise straight away. Setting\na new visit context makes the patient chart relaunch its workspace group\nonce the visit is refetched, and the relaunch closes every open window, so\nthe resumed workspace was closed before it rendered. The RDE-off path\nwould hit the same thing once the callback is wired up.\n\nThe patient chart store now records which visit the workspace group was\nlast launched with, and the chart sets it after each successful relaunch.\nuseStartVisitIfNeeded resolves true only once that matches the new visit\ncontext. Under RDE, closing the switcher after a selection no longer\nresolves false first.\n\n* Check that the visit note opens after starting a visit from the prompt\n\nThe visit context test already opens the visit note from the side rail\nwith no visit, starts a visit from the prompt, and waits for the Active\nVisit tag. It now also checks that the visit note form opens by itself\nand can still be written in once the chart has picked up the new visit,\nthen discards the note so the later delete visit steps start clean.\n\n* Resolve every pending visit prompt once the workspace group has the visit\n\nuseStartVisitIfNeeded kept a single pending resolver per hook instance, so\nif the same caller had two prompts comp","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":["O3-5998"],"pullRequests":[3688],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"4d9f19a2d629347559fe32b89899af6245c16e23","date":"2026-09-24T15:31:10.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5989: Keep a visit note saved when one of its images is rejected (#3670)","message":"(fix) O3-5989: Keep a visit note saved when one of its images is rejected (#3670)\n\nBy the time the images upload, the note and its diagnoses are already on\nthe server. A rejected image used to bubble into the catch handler, which\nshowed \"Error saving visit note\" and left the form open in create mode, so\nthe next Save and close posted a second note.\n\nUploads now run with Promise.allSettled. Every image the server accepts is\nsaved, the workspace closes as usual, and a warning snackbar names the\nimages that were rejected with the server's reason, pointing the user at\nthe note to add them again. A failure to save the note itself still shows\nthe error and keeps the form open.","ticketKeys":["O3-5989"],"pullRequests":[3670],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"52ad5642b88661b759f5e130f12e1d73a7fac66a","date":"2026-09-23T08:32:38.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)","message":"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)\n\n* fix: O3-5990 Remove saved visit-note images safely\n\nConfirm removal of a saved image and void its observation through the obs endpoint. This preserves the encounter and diagnoses when the image is the only observation. Refresh attachment, note, and visit data after removal.\n\nExplain that removal takes effect immediately and discarding note edits will not restore the image. Cover cancel, success, and retry after failure. Verify that a blank note and its diagnosis survive removal of the sole image in the local browser and backend.\n\n* style: Put React first in image removal test imports\n\nMove the React import above the test utilities in the saved-image removal modal test.\n\n* fix: Save visit-note image removals with the form\n\nKeep image removals pending until Save and close, with Undo and Discard restoring the draft. Show a dimmed thumbnail and a separate Undo action for images marked for removal.\n\nRetry failed removals without repeating successful deletions, and avoid rewriting the note when only images change. Keep the visit-context header state stable during form updates.\n\n* fix: Refresh visit-note data once per save attempt\n\nRefresh after the removal batch and note save, including partial failures. Add coverage for saved diagnoses and successful and failed removal batches.\n\nSimplify the image markup, separate the error title from its explanation, and remove redundant footer styles.","ticketKeys":["O3-5990"],"pullRequests":[3684],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"96b812bb0206c034792895cacfad69dd3f37b44a","date":"2026-09-18T20:42:17.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5986: Show a visit note's saved images when editing it (#3668)","message":"(fix) O3-5986: Show a visit note's saved images when editing it (#3668)\n\nImages added to a visit note are uploaded with the note's encounter UUID, and the edit form loads and shows the attachments recorded on that encounter, read only. Only images added in the session live in form state, so a text-only edit uploads nothing. Attachment obs in the Visits page encounter expansion render as caption or file-name links that open a new read-only attachment-preview-modal, and the bytes URL helper moves to esm-patient-common-lib. Depends on openmrs/openmrs-esm-core#1887. Follow-ups: O3-5987, O3-5988, O3-5989, O3-5990.","ticketKeys":["O3-5986","O3-5987","O3-5988","O3-5989","O3-5990"],"pullRequests":[3668],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","hash":"fb886e7a893d1638bb65ea0136967c99029ac54b","date":"2026-09-18T17:22:04.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(feat) O3-5986: Let attachments be recorded on and read by encounter (#1887)","message":"(feat) O3-5986: Let attachments be recorded on and read by encounter (#1887)\n\n* (feat) O3-5986: Let attachments be recorded on and read by encounter\n\ncreateAttachment now takes an optional encounter UUID and sends it as the\n`encounter` form field. That lets the visit note form record an image on the\nnote's own encounter instead of leaving it encounterless, which is why saved\nimages never show up again when we reopen the note.\n\ngetAttachments and useAttachments take the same optional UUID and hit\n`/attachment?patient=...&encounter=...` when it's set. We leave\nincludeEncounterless out of that request on purpose: the attachments module\nignores the encounter filter whenever includeEncounterless is present. Both\ngo through a new getAttachmentsUrl helper so the fetch and the SWR cache key\nare always the same string, and consumers can build that key when they need\nto invalidate it.\n\nExisting callers are unchanged. Adds the first tests for these helpers,\nmirrors the helper in the emr-api and storybook mocks and regenerates the\nAPI docs.\n\n* Skip the attachments fetch while the patient UUID is empty\n\nuseAttachments now passes a null SWR key when patientUuid is falsy, the same\nway usePatient does, so a form can defer the request until it knows which\nencounter to load.\n\n* Warn about unresolvable encounter UUIDs in the attachment docs\n\nThe attachments module resolves the encounter param with getEncounterByUuid\nand, when that yields null with no includeEncounterless flag, falls back to\nevery attachment of the patient. Callers should only pass an encounter UUID\nthey have already loaded.","ticketKeys":["O3-5986"],"pullRequests":[1887],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-attachments","hash":"3a43eff9ad45541e17dca0cb4c373636eaa06218","date":"2026-09-18T01:35:03.000Z","author":"Wikum Weerakutti","subject":"ATT-65: Fix Saving a visit note with multiple image attachments fails (#92)","message":"ATT-65: Fix Saving a visit note with multiple image attachments fails (#92)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[92],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"385d75cc2bbcc2a6802ca4f96dde611072cd4dec","date":"2026-09-17T18:05:49.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Preserve visit note image changes and improve removal controls (#3663)","message":"(fix) Preserve visit note image changes and improve removal controls (#3663)\n\n* fix: preserve visit note image changes and improve removal controls\n\nTrack image additions and removals as form changes and read the current images for each upload callback so batches retain every file. Use labelled, contrasting remove buttons that do not submit the form. Cover create and edit workflows, batch uploads and removal.\n\n* fix: preserve image remove button contrast across interaction states\n\nSet explicit hover, focus and active colours so Carbon secondary button styles cannot hide the close icon. Remove the redundant button type, which Carbon already defaults to button.\n\n* fix: identify images in visit note removal labels\n\nUse the image description, filename or image number in each remove button's accessible name. Update the translation and tests to cover the fallbacks and select the intended image by name.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3663],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"e8bf5eeaa08a65b4b8b1845e4ca1a224f3f90790","date":"2026-09-14T10:31:33.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)","message":"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)\n\n* (fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form\n\nMake condition search results keyboard accessible with visible focus and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep the selected condition name in the input.\n\nUse Record condition for creation and Edit condition for editing. Update translations and cover keyboard navigation and workspace titles in component and browser tests.\n\n* Remove unused conditions workspace title prop\n\nThe conditions form sets its edit title on Workspace2. Remove the unused launch prop and translation dependency, and update the action menu test to match.\n\n* Keep condition search focus when results refresh\n\nReturn focus to the search input when loading removes a focused result. Leave focus alone when the user has moved elsewhere, and test that keyboard input continues in the intended field.","ticketKeys":["O3-5969"],"pullRequests":[3646],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"6961c3d13e74a69bc2ed96dc3fa5aa1cc4d86f25","date":"2026-09-11T21:11:25.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)","message":"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)\n\n* (fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes\n\nMake diagnosis search results keyboard accessible and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep tablet row padding on the result button so its click target and focus outline fill the row.\n\nUse Add visit note and Edit visit note consistently in workspace titles and tablet headings. Update translations and cover the keyboard flow and titles in component and browser tests.\n\n* Update visit context test for the add visit note title\n\nThe siderail opens the note workspace in creation mode. Expect Add visit note so the visit context test matches the renamed workspace title.\n\n* Keep diagnosis search focus when results refresh\n\nReturn focus to the corresponding diagnosis input when loading removes a focused result. Preserve focus when the user moves elsewhere, and cover continued typing in both diagnosis searches and the notes field.\n\n* Reduce spacing below open diagnosis results\n\nUse a smaller bottom margin while diagnosis results are visible. Keep the existing spacing when the list is closed. Verified desktop and tablet layouts and the visit-note E2E workflow.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3645],"linksSource":"message, unverified"}],"filters":{"repos":["github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-core","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-billing-app","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-cohortbuilder-app","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-fast-data-entry-app","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-builder","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-laboratory-app","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management-app","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-user-onboarding-app","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-addresshierarchy","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-attachments","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-authentication","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-bedmanagement","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-billing","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-calculation","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-cohort","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-emrapi","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-event","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-fhir2","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-htmlwidgets","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-idgen","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-legacyui","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-metadataexport","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-metadatamapping","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-o3forms","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-openconceptlab","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-ordertemplates","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-patientdocuments","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-patientflags","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-queue","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-reporting","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-reportingrest","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-serialization.xstream","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-stockmanagement","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-tasks","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-webservices.rest"],"revisions":["HEAD"],"messageTerms":["visit note","conditions","diagnos"],"count":50},"coverageGaps":[],"truncated":["commits: showing 50 of 235 found","commits: answer byte cap reached; showing 15 of 235 found"]}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8a41210-13c5-40eb-88d8-295f472700ba","uuid":"b5ae10a9-9f16-4326-a4e8-e968ece81851","timestamp":"2026-10-31T15:31:44.303Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"d0f4b1bf5be04ad6f9c567635864b36de6ac36c3","date":"2026-10-07T13:20:03.000Z","author":"Veronica Mukuhi Muthee","subject":"(feat) O3-5823: Capture diagnosis rank and certainty in the visit note (#3621)","message":"(feat) O3-5823: Capture diagnosis rank and certainty in the visit note (#3621)","ticketKeys":["O3-5823"],"pullRequests":[3621],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","hash":"0e1edc234479890d45bc09e67b2ee25befc1c803","date":"2026-10-05T11:52:41.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-6027: Clear order and diagnosis submissions on every write (#826)","message":"(fix) O3-6027: Clear order and diagnosis submissions on every write (#826)\n\n* (fix) Clear order and diagnosis submissions on every write\n\nOrdersAdapter and EncounterDiagnosisAdapter now clear the field's\nsubmission at the start of transformFieldValue, the same way ObsAdapter\nalready does.\n\ngracefullySetSubmission only sets values and never clears them, so a\nnewValue from an earlier write stayed on the field after it was\ncleared. On a new encounter, selecting an order or diagnosis and then\nclearing the field still submitted it. On an edited encounter, swapping\na stored order or diagnosis for another value and then clearing the\nfield still submitted the swapped value: a NEW order alongside the\nvoid, or an edit of the stored diagnosis to the swapped concept.\nClearing first means nothing is submitted for a new encounter and only\nthe void goes out for an edited one.\n\neditOrder no longer needs its own clearSubmission call when the value\nmatches the stored order, since the submission is already empty.\n\n* Fixup","ticketKeys":["O3-6027"],"pullRequests":[826],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-bedmanagement","hash":"a6aa20a5afb9ee7b9fa2fd2eac251e36455b10d2","date":"2026-10-05T10:22:50.000Z","author":"Ken Omondi","subject":"BED-40: Ending a visit with no bed assignment must not require bed write privileges (#119)","message":"BED-40: Ending a visit with no bed assignment must not require bed write privileges (#119)\n\n* BED-40: ending a visit with no bed assignment must not require bed write privileges\n\nVisitWithBedPatientAssignmentSaveHandler called unAssignBedsInEndedVisit on\nevery save of an ended visit. That method requires \"Assign Beds\" and\n\"Edit Admission Locations\", so a user who may end visits but not manage beds\ngot an APIAuthenticationException even when the patient never had a bed.\n\nOnly call it when the visit has an active bed assignment. Ending a visit\nthat does hold a bed still requires both privileges.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PLmE4JrqYk2DTfmUfu4SqY\n\n* BED-40: merge the end-visit condition into one if statement\n\nSonarCloud flagged the nested if (java:S1066). The three conditions are now\none if, in the same short-circuit order, so the bed lookup still runs only\nfor a persisted, ended visit. Behaviour is unchanged; api 124, atom-feed 5\nand omod 41 tests pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PLmE4JrqYk2DTfmUfu4SqY\n\n* BED-40: wrap the comment so the formatter keeps it, and commit the formatted tests\n\nThe comment is wrapped as suggested in review, so the formatter that runs at\ncompile leaves it whole. The two test classes are committed as the formatter\nwrites them, so a build changes none of the three files.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[119],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","hash":"ebb02b719931d121419669b531b6e05c77f515e9","date":"2026-10-02T18:57:25.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-6030: Keep hidden obs group members, orders and diagnoses out of submissions (#822)","message":"(fix) O3-6030: Keep hidden obs group members, orders and diagnoses out of submissions (#822)\n\n* (fix) Keep hidden obs group members, orders and diagnoses out of submissions\n\nHide logic only kept hidden top-level obs out of the encounter payload.\nHidden obs group members, test orders and diagnoses kept whatever value\nwas entered before the field was hidden, so they were still submitted\neven though the form no longer showed them.\n\nprocessObsGroup now skips hidden members and, in edit mode, voids their\nstored obs, the same way top-level obs are handled. It reads each\nmember's visibility and stored obs from the flattened form field,\nbecause hide evaluation and hydration update that copy rather than the\none held in the group's questions. prepareOrders and prepareDiagnosis\nnow skip hidden fields.\n\n* Evaluate hide logic for repeated field instances\n\nRows added to a repeating field kept their hidden state from when they\nwere created, so hiding a repeating test order, diagnosis or obs group\nmember left its extra rows in the encounter payload. Extra group rows\nalso stayed visible in the form.\n\nfindFieldSection looks up the field's page through meta.pageId, which\nrepeated instances don't carry because cloneRepeatField replaces their\nmeta. Reading sections off the missing page threw inside the\nfieldDependents loop in handleFieldLogic, so none of the repeated\ninstances had their hide expression re-evaluated. It now returns\nundefined when the page isn't found, which skips the section visibility\nupdate for repeated instances since they aren't in the form schema.\n\n* (fix) Preserve pending deletions for hidden orders and diagnoses\n\nFiltering hidden fields out of encounter submissions discarded explicit deletions when a previously cleared field became hidden. Keep pending voided values for hidden orders and diagnoses while excluding their new values. Leave stored values untouched when no deletion is pending, and preserve existing submission behavior for visible fields.\n\n* Skip delete","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":["O3-6030"],"pullRequests":[822],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","hash":"f8aa79f6e3c0814d0f9bf8449fb79dbe08558dd0","date":"2026-10-02T17:36:05.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(feat) O3-5823: Add certainty display and blue/gray defaults to diagnosis tags (#1881)","message":"(feat) O3-5823: Add certainty display and blue/gray defaults to diagnosis tags (#1881)","ticketKeys":["O3-5823"],"pullRequests":[1881],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"a0834be003ea69917f36dac8b4bccba52ba8a7a4","date":"2026-10-02T05:50:44.000Z","author":"chibongho","subject":"(fix) O3-6020: Make Visit Notes workspace accept an Encounter object for editing (#3719)","message":"(fix) O3-6020: Make Visit Notes workspace accept an Encounter object for editing (#3719)\n\n* (fix) O3-6020: Make Visit Notes workspace accept a Encounter object for editing\n\n* address feedback\n\n---------","ticketKeys":["O3-6020"],"pullRequests":[3719],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"108c48985b5e33905d025cb936a5657f45bb7a7a","date":"2026-09-24T20:50:01.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5998: Continue to the requested workspace after starting or selecting a visit (#3688)","message":"(fix) O3-5998: Continue to the requested workspace after starting or selecting a visit (#3688)\n\n* (fix) O3-5998: Continue to the requested workspace after starting or selecting a visit\n\nWhen a chart action needs a visit and the patient has none,\nuseStartVisitIfNeeded shows a visit prompt and waits for the user to start\nor pick a visit. Neither path continued to the workspace the user asked\nfor, so they had to click the action again.\n\nWith RDE off, the start visit dialog passes onVisitStarted into the\nstart-visit-workspace-form workspace, but the chart's wrapper for that\nworkspace never read it, so the promise never resolved. The wrapper now\naccepts onVisitStarted and calls it after it sets the visit context.\n\nWith RDE on, selecting a visit resolved the promise straight away. Setting\na new visit context makes the patient chart relaunch its workspace group\nonce the visit is refetched, and the relaunch closes every open window, so\nthe resumed workspace was closed before it rendered. The RDE-off path\nwould hit the same thing once the callback is wired up.\n\nThe patient chart store now records which visit the workspace group was\nlast launched with, and the chart sets it after each successful relaunch.\nuseStartVisitIfNeeded resolves true only once that matches the new visit\ncontext. Under RDE, closing the switcher after a selection no longer\nresolves false first.\n\n* Check that the visit note opens after starting a visit from the prompt\n\nThe visit context test already opens the visit note from the side rail\nwith no visit, starts a visit from the prompt, and waits for the Active\nVisit tag. It now also checks that the visit note form opens by itself\nand can still be written in once the chart has picked up the new visit,\nthen discards the note so the later delete visit steps start clean.\n\n* Resolve every pending visit prompt once the workspace group has the visit\n\nuseStartVisitIfNeeded kept a single pending resolver per hook instance, so\nif the same caller had two prompts comp","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":["O3-5998"],"pullRequests":[3688],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"4d9f19a2d629347559fe32b89899af6245c16e23","date":"2026-09-24T15:31:10.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5989: Keep a visit note saved when one of its images is rejected (#3670)","message":"(fix) O3-5989: Keep a visit note saved when one of its images is rejected (#3670)\n\nBy the time the images upload, the note and its diagnoses are already on\nthe server. A rejected image used to bubble into the catch handler, which\nshowed \"Error saving visit note\" and left the form open in create mode, so\nthe next Save and close posted a second note.\n\nUploads now run with Promise.allSettled. Every image the server accepts is\nsaved, the workspace closes as usual, and a warning snackbar names the\nimages that were rejected with the server's reason, pointing the user at\nthe note to add them again. A failure to save the note itself still shows\nthe error and keeps the form open.","ticketKeys":["O3-5989"],"pullRequests":[3670],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"52ad5642b88661b759f5e130f12e1d73a7fac66a","date":"2026-09-23T08:32:38.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)","message":"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)\n\n* fix: O3-5990 Remove saved visit-note images safely\n\nConfirm removal of a saved image and void its observation through the obs endpoint. This preserves the encounter and diagnoses when the image is the only observation. Refresh attachment, note, and visit data after removal.\n\nExplain that removal takes effect immediately and discarding note edits will not restore the image. Cover cancel, success, and retry after failure. Verify that a blank note and its diagnosis survive removal of the sole image in the local browser and backend.\n\n* style: Put React first in image removal test imports\n\nMove the React import above the test utilities in the saved-image removal modal test.\n\n* fix: Save visit-note image removals with the form\n\nKeep image removals pending until Save and close, with Undo and Discard restoring the draft. Show a dimmed thumbnail and a separate Undo action for images marked for removal.\n\nRetry failed removals without repeating successful deletions, and avoid rewriting the note when only images change. Keep the visit-context header state stable during form updates.\n\n* fix: Refresh visit-note data once per save attempt\n\nRefresh after the removal batch and note save, including partial failures. Add coverage for saved diagnoses and successful and failed removal batches.\n\nSimplify the image markup, separate the error title from its explanation, and remove redundant footer styles.","ticketKeys":["O3-5990"],"pullRequests":[3684],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"96b812bb0206c034792895cacfad69dd3f37b44a","date":"2026-09-18T20:42:17.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5986: Show a visit note's saved images when editing it (#3668)","message":"(fix) O3-5986: Show a visit note's saved images when editing it (#3668)\n\nImages added to a visit note are uploaded with the note's encounter UUID, and the edit form loads and shows the attachments recorded on that encounter, read only. Only images added in the session live in form state, so a text-only edit uploads nothing. Attachment obs in the Visits page encounter expansion render as caption or file-name links that open a new read-only attachment-preview-modal, and the bytes URL helper moves to esm-patient-common-lib. Depends on openmrs/openmrs-esm-core#1887. Follow-ups: O3-5987, O3-5988, O3-5989, O3-5990.","ticketKeys":["O3-5986","O3-5987","O3-5988","O3-5989","O3-5990"],"pullRequests":[3668],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","hash":"fb886e7a893d1638bb65ea0136967c99029ac54b","date":"2026-09-18T17:22:04.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(feat) O3-5986: Let attachments be recorded on and read by encounter (#1887)","message":"(feat) O3-5986: Let attachments be recorded on and read by encounter (#1887)\n\n* (feat) O3-5986: Let attachments be recorded on and read by encounter\n\ncreateAttachment now takes an optional encounter UUID and sends it as the\n`encounter` form field. That lets the visit note form record an image on the\nnote's own encounter instead of leaving it encounterless, which is why saved\nimages never show up again when we reopen the note.\n\ngetAttachments and useAttachments take the same optional UUID and hit\n`/attachment?patient=...&encounter=...` when it's set. We leave\nincludeEncounterless out of that request on purpose: the attachments module\nignores the encounter filter whenever includeEncounterless is present. Both\ngo through a new getAttachmentsUrl helper so the fetch and the SWR cache key\nare always the same string, and consumers can build that key when they need\nto invalidate it.\n\nExisting callers are unchanged. Adds the first tests for these helpers,\nmirrors the helper in the emr-api and storybook mocks and regenerates the\nAPI docs.\n\n* Skip the attachments fetch while the patient UUID is empty\n\nuseAttachments now passes a null SWR key when patientUuid is falsy, the same\nway usePatient does, so a form can defer the request until it knows which\nencounter to load.\n\n* Warn about unresolvable encounter UUIDs in the attachment docs\n\nThe attachments module resolves the encounter param with getEncounterByUuid\nand, when that yields null with no includeEncounterless flag, falls back to\nevery attachment of the patient. Callers should only pass an encounter UUID\nthey have already loaded.","ticketKeys":["O3-5986"],"pullRequests":[1887],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-attachments","hash":"3a43eff9ad45541e17dca0cb4c373636eaa06218","date":"2026-09-18T01:35:03.000Z","author":"Wikum Weerakutti","subject":"ATT-65: Fix Saving a visit note with multiple image attachments fails (#92)","message":"ATT-65: Fix Saving a visit note with multiple image attachments fails (#92)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[92],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"385d75cc2bbcc2a6802ca4f96dde611072cd4dec","date":"2026-09-17T18:05:49.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Preserve visit note image changes and improve removal controls (#3663)","message":"(fix) Preserve visit note image changes and improve removal controls (#3663)\n\n* fix: preserve visit note image changes and improve removal controls\n\nTrack image additions and removals as form changes and read the current images for each upload callback so batches retain every file. Use labelled, contrasting remove buttons that do not submit the form. Cover create and edit workflows, batch uploads and removal.\n\n* fix: preserve image remove button contrast across interaction states\n\nSet explicit hover, focus and active colours so Carbon secondary button styles cannot hide the close icon. Remove the redundant button type, which Carbon already defaults to button.\n\n* fix: identify images in visit note removal labels\n\nUse the image description, filename or image number in each remove button's accessible name. Update the translation and tests to cover the fallbacks and select the intended image by name.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3663],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"e8bf5eeaa08a65b4b8b1845e4ca1a224f3f90790","date":"2026-09-14T10:31:33.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)","message":"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)\n\n* (fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form\n\nMake condition search results keyboard accessible with visible focus and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep the selected condition name in the input.\n\nUse Record condition for creation and Edit condition for editing. Update translations and cover keyboard navigation and workspace titles in component and browser tests.\n\n* Remove unused conditions workspace title prop\n\nThe conditions form sets its edit title on Workspace2. Remove the unused launch prop and translation dependency, and update the action menu test to match.\n\n* Keep condition search focus when results refresh\n\nReturn focus to the search input when loading removes a focused result. Leave focus alone when the user has moved elsewhere, and test that keyboard input continues in the intended field.","ticketKeys":["O3-5969"],"pullRequests":[3646],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"6961c3d13e74a69bc2ed96dc3fa5aa1cc4d86f25","date":"2026-09-11T21:11:25.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)","message":"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)\n\n* (fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes\n\nMake diagnosis search results keyboard accessible and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep tablet row padding on the result button so its click target and focus outline fill the row.\n\nUse Add visit note and Edit visit note consistently in workspace titles and tablet headings. Update translations and cover the keyboard flow and titles in component and browser tests.\n\n* Update visit context test for the add visit note title\n\nThe siderail opens the note workspace in creation mode. Expect Add visit note so the visit context test matches the renamed workspace title.\n\n* Keep diagnosis search focus when results refresh\n\nReturn focus to the corresponding diagnosis input when loading removes a focused result. Preserve focus when the user moves elsewhere, and cover continued typing in both diagnosis searches and the notes field.\n\n* Reduce spacing below open diagnosis results\n\nUse a smaller bottom margin while diagnosis results are visible. Keep the existing spacing when the list is closed. Verified desktop and tablet layouts and the visit-note E2E workflow.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3645],"linksSource":"message, unverified"}],"filters":{"repos":["github.com/openmrs/openmrs-contrib-o3-docs","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-core","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-billing-app","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-cohortbuilder-app","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-dispensing-app","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-fast-data-entry-app","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-builder","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-laboratory-app","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-stock-management-app","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-user-onboarding-app","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-addresshierarchy","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-attachments","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-authentication","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-bedmanagement","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-billing","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-calculation","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-cohort","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-emrapi","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-event","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-fhir2","github.com/openmrs/openmrs