{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NH2WtjB5DVf2BkmNDpk6C3","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"e8bf5eeaa08a65b4b8b1845e4ca1a224f3f90790","date":"2026-09-14T10:31:33.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)","message":"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)\n\n* (fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form\n\nMake condition search results keyboard accessible with visible focus and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep the selected condition name in the input.\n\nUse Record condition for creation and Edit condition for editing. Update translations and cover keyboard navigation and workspace titles in component and browser tests.\n\n* Remove unused conditions workspace title prop\n\nThe conditions form sets its edit title on Workspace2. Remove the unused launch prop and translation dependency, and update the action menu test to match.\n\n* Keep condition search focus when results refresh\n\nReturn focus to the search input when loading removes a focused result. Leave focus alone when the user has moved elsewhere, and test that keyboard input continues in the intended field.","ticketKeys":["O3-5969"],"pullRequests":[3646],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","hash":"6ec18930c2e6e6d7b7ba9062c015114547be9806","date":"2026-09-11T19:55:33.000Z","author":"Ian","subject":"(fix) Move hard lifecycle stop to framework instead of single-spa (#1867)","message":"(fix) Move hard lifecycle stop to framework instead of single-spa (#1867)\n\n* (fix) Move hard lifecycle stop to framework instead of single-spa\n\nsingle-spa's \"timeouts\" actually become `setTimeout()` calls that are\nnot cleared, even when the event they are waiting for has already\nhappened. The upshot of this is that pushing the 15s hard timeout for\nlifecycles to single-spa wound up holding references to unmounted apps\nunconditionally for 15s, even after the actual contents had unmounted.\n\nBy moving the hard timeouts into our framework and reverting to\nsingle-spa's defaults, we greatly reduce the window that single-spa will\nhold the references to its default of 3s. Short of patching single-spa,\nthis seems like the best way we can work around this issue.\n\n* Create changeset\n\n* Address review feedback\n\n* (chore) Add docs\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: openmrs-bot <infrastructure@openmrs.org>","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[1867],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","hash":"818b3b6fe433f1e3da65f25857866fd9308851bb","date":"2026-09-10T18:20:35.000Z","author":"Ian","subject":"(BREAKING) Switch from the style-loader to CSS loader in production mode (#1869)","message":"(BREAKING) Switch from the style-loader to CSS loader in production mode (#1869)\n\n* (feat) Switch from the style-loader to CSS loader in production mode\n\nThis is the implementation of RFC-0033, removing our use of CSS-in-JS\nfrom apps and the framework. In order to keep the output of both rspack\nand webpack in sync, it implements a slightly larger surface than expected,\nbasically ensuring we're using a consistent browserlist.\n\nThis also removes the \"main\" chunk we were generating, but which was\nunreachable, since our entry point was always the module federation\nloader and then the index chunk.\n\nFinally, this adds a rspack / webpack plugin to enforce the rule that an\napp must not change global styles of Carbon components, but may make any\nadjustments provided those are appropriately scoped.\n\n* Add integration test covering CSS assets\n\n* Support data-extension-* as valid targeted selectors\n\n* Address code review comments and align with JS branch\n\n* Up the test timeout for integration tests\n\n* Create changeset\n\n* Fix failing test on CI","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[1869],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"324603e9b2d62756416654585d2e6c1d1653fa14","date":"2026-09-01T20:29:42.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label (#3612)","message":"(fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label (#3612)\n\n* (fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label\n\nOn @carbon/react 1.x, the classic OverflowMenu pulls aria-label out of its props and applies it to the menu body (the ul with role menu), not to the trigger button. The trigger's accessible name comes from iconDescription, which defaults to 'Options'. Every overflow menu in this repo passed its label via aria-label, so screen readers announced a generic 'Options' for all of them.\n\nPass the label through iconDescription instead in the visit timeline, encounters table, orders and medications tables, and the allergies, conditions, procedures, programs, and vitals action menus. The conditions menu label was a hardcoded string, so it is now translated. Unit tests and e2e specs that located the triggers by the 'Options' name now use the real labels.\n\n* Keep aria-label on overflow menus so the popup stays named\n\nCarbon's classic OverflowMenu applies aria-label to the opened menu body (the ul with role menu), so dropping it left the popup without an accessible name. Keep aria-label alongside iconDescription so the trigger and the popup are both named. The encounters table test now asserts the popup's aria-label.\n\n* Disambiguate the delete confirmation locators in the e2e specs\n\nThe allergies, biometrics, and vitals trigger names now contain the word delete, so the modal confirmation locator getByRole('button', { name: /delete/i }) matched two elements and failed in strict mode. Target the modal's danger button instead, matching the existing conditions spec.\n\n* Cover the remaining overflow menu labels\n\nName the procedures, attachment preview, and clinical encounter list menus consistently. Remove the misplaced attachment menu item label and cover the accessible names in focused tests.\n\n* Update the procedures and attachments e2e locators for the new trigger names\n\nThe procedures and attachment preview triggers a","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3612],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","hash":"a9fdbfc0f5c2a09368c3fb6e777fc3c274629f76","date":"2026-07-16T13:02:24.000Z","author":"denniskigen","subject":"(fix) Only render diagnosis code span when a code exists","message":"(fix) Only render diagnosis code span when a code exists\n\nFollow-up to #767. Diagnoses without a terminology mapping rendered an\nempty code span with a reserved 4rem column, indenting their labels to\nmatch coded entries. Render the code span conditionally instead so\ncodeless diagnoses display without the placeholder gap.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"64d3c9902168b1a43b08d5da09558e7da6288a0d","date":"2026-06-19T13:21:12.000Z","author":"Nethmi Rodrigo","subject":"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)","message":"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3403],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"bd0350391135e8e0cb8ac61cabd0e3ce5256b28d","date":"2026-06-09T13:10:29.000Z","author":"sfortune","subject":"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)","message":"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)\n\nfix(O3-5709): use table-of-contents icon for Conditions to distinguish from task list\n\nThe Conditions item in the patient chart's left nav and the Task list in\nthe right rail both rendered omrs-icon-list-checked, falsely implying a\nsemantic link between a longitudinal clinical problem list and operational\naction items.\n\nSwitch Conditions to omrs-icon-table-of-contents, an already-registered,\nunclaimed glyph that reads as a list without the checklist connotation. This\nis an interim fix: the durable solution is a dedicated Conditions glyph in\nesm-styleguide (so ConditionsIcon stops aliasing ListCheckedIcon), tracked\nunder O3-5709.\n\nCo-authored-by: denniskigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","ticketKeys":["O3-5709"],"pullRequests":[3359],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","hash":"f36d54777376cc8ce804cc10db6b7ff7da498536","date":"2026-05-29T13:41:24.000Z","author":"denniskigen","subject":"(fix) Add patient procedures app to e2e environment","message":"(fix) Add patient procedures app to e2e environment\n\nThe downstream e2e job (run-e2e-on-other-repos) serves a hardcoded set of\nfrontend modules assembled in run-e2e-docker-env.sh, then runs each\ndownstream repo's specs against it. patient-chart added procedures.spec.ts\n(#3338), which navigates to /chart/procedures and waits for the \"Record\nprocedures\" button rendered by @openmrs/esm-patient-procedures-app.\n\nThat app was missing from the assembled import map, so the dashboard never\nrendered and the spec hit the 180s timeout on every run, including main.\nThe stuck test also held a Playwright worker for the full timeout, which\nintermittently tipped the conditions and vitals form-launch specs over\ntheir own timeouts.\n\nAdd the procedures app so the spec can run. The backend image\n(reference-application-3-backend:nightly-with-data) already carries the\nprocedure concepts, as patient-chart's own e2e passes the full spec.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"3568fa685f2d33a17b6fb975b089ed4b0abb5cfe","date":"2026-05-17T21:37:59.000Z","author":"denniskigen","subject":"fix: prevent escaped condition duplicate warnings","message":"fix: prevent escaped condition duplicate warnings","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"05cfbca7dbdd7488e868e1ffcb5d1ff0a00aac8b","date":"2026-04-30T10:50:10.000Z","author":"Skengmann","subject":"(fix) Correct casing of editCondition label (#3170)","message":"(fix) Correct casing of editCondition label (#3170)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3170],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"c7c10df4f1bec30712d71b2557e3222251827436","date":"2026-04-30T10:04:20.000Z","author":"Devarasetty Praneeth","subject":"(fix) O3-5444: Show inline warning when adding a duplicate condition (#3227)","message":"(fix) O3-5444: Show inline warning when adding a duplicate condition (#3227)","ticketKeys":["O3-5444"],"pullRequests":[3227],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"d92a26c2a1c087c33f22cee56bf2b07c5eb96495","date":"2026-04-22T20:56:54.000Z","author":"omeri innocent","subject":"(fix) O3-5614: Fix delete-condition retry and conditions search input (#3254)","message":"(fix) O3-5614: Fix delete-condition retry and conditions search input (#3254)","ticketKeys":["O3-5614"],"pullRequests":[3254],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"2c514a99a75389e9ccf680a9584eb68db57a2267","date":"2026-04-21T11:18:02.000Z","author":"Om Srivastava","subject":"(fix) O3-5618: Validate condition selection before submit triggers (#3240)","message":"(fix) O3-5618: Validate condition selection before submit triggers (#3240)","ticketKeys":["O3-5618"],"pullRequests":[3240],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"7fa740c199cb105713451efcc641d0a250b0ef59","date":"2026-04-01T21:20:31.000Z","author":"solomonfortune","subject":"(feat) O3-5580: Default clinical status to active when recording a new condition (#3195)","message":"(feat) O3-5580: Default clinical status to active when recording a new condition (#3195)","ticketKeys":["O3-5580"],"pullRequests":[3195],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"7f324ebd5b575f0bbb5868d71a7245c9957eeaba","date":"2026-03-19T13:01:47.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Improve drug order workspace UX (#3138)","message":"(fix) Improve drug order workspace UX (#3138)\n\n- Preserve search term when navigating back from the order form\n- Cancel on new orders returns to drug search instead of closing the workspace\n- Auto-focus the drug search input\n- Hide dose section in order basket tile when dosage is null\n- Fix conditional separators in order basket tile to avoid dangling dashes\n- Allow long drug names to wrap instead of clipping in order basket tiles\n- Remove redundant validation error snackbar from drug order form\n- Remove unused imports and translation keys","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3138],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"b2270525c8afea42e924e28916c44fa398fef91c","date":"2026-03-09T15:30:10.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Treat zero as a valid vitals value instead of falsy/empty (#3084)","message":"(fix) Treat zero as a valid vitals value instead of falsy/empty (#3084)\n\n* (fix) Treat zero as a valid vitals value instead of falsy/empty\n\nJavaScript treats 0 as falsy, which caused zero-valued vitals to be\nsilently skipped across the entire pipeline — fetching, display,\nflagging, validation, and persistence.\n\nReplace all truthiness checks (if (value), Boolean(value), value && ...)\nwith explicit null checks (value != null && value !== '') so that 0 is\ntreated as a real recorded value while undefined, null, and empty strings\ncontinue to mean \"no value\".\n\nAffected layers:\n- assessValue: 0 is now evaluated against reference ranges and flagged\n- prepareObsForSubmission: 0-valued obs are created; editing to 0 no\n  longer voids the old obs without creating a replacement\n- data.resource: 0-valued FHIR observations are no longer dropped from\n  the encounter hash table\n- VitalsHeaderItem: 0 displays with its unit instead of \"Not available\"\n- vitals-header.extension: unit symbols render for 0-valued vitals\n- Form workspace: interpretation and range validation run for 0 values\n- Schema: a form with only a 0-valued field passes \"at least one field\"\n- Input validity: typing 0 is no longer flagged as invalid input\n\n* (fix) Address review feedback: null-check range thresholds and MUAC conditional\n\n- assessValue: use != null for range threshold checks (hiCritical,\n  hiNormal, lowCritical, lowNormal) so a threshold of 0 is not skipped\n- vitals header: use != null for MUAC conditional rendering for\n  consistency with the rest of the patch","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3084],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"ac1012bafec8f832c80d5557bc5e818f8e2143ee","date":"2026-03-04T19:01:35.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Improve E2E test reliability (#3067)","message":"(fix) Improve E2E test reliability (#3067)\n\n* (fix) Improve E2E test reliability\n\nReplace fragile locators and fix test infrastructure issues that cause\nintermittent E2E failures.\n\nSelectors:\n- Replace .nth(0) positional selectors with row-scoped locators\n  (dataRow, getByRole('row').filter()) across allergies, biometrics,\n  conditions, drug-orders, lab-orders, results-viewer, visit-note, and\n  vitals specs\n- Replace CSS class selectors ([class*=\"previewContainer\"]) with\n  role-based locators in attachment preview tests\n- Use getByLabel instead of getByText for form input fields in\n  drug-orders\n- Add role=\"dialog\" and aria-label to attachment preview component\n  for stable test targeting\n\nAssertions:\n- Replace snapshot assertions (textContent + expect) with auto-retrying\n  Playwright assertions (toHaveText, toHaveValue) in edit-existing-visit\n- Wrap bare .isVisible() calls with expect() in immunizations\n- Add missing await on visitsPage.goTo() in results-viewer\n- Remove swallowed .catch(() => {}) on assertion in attachments\n\nTest state:\n- Convert module-level mutable state to per-test fixtures in\n  drug-orders and lab-orders specs (retry/parallel safe)\n- Use test patient fixture instead of manual creation in\n  visit-context-navigation\n- Add try/finally with null guards for cleanup of manually created\n  resources\n\nCleanup helpers:\n- Add response status assertions to deleteEncounter, deleteDrugOrder,\n  deleteTestOrder (accept 200/204/400/404/500)\n- Add ok() assertion to endVisit (accept 200/400 for already-ended\n  visits) and getVisit\n- Remove unnecessary empty request bodies from delete helpers\n\nDrug order recording:\n- Handle environment differences where the order basket may open the\n  drug search workspace directly or require an additional click\n\n* Drop status assertions from delete cleanup helpers\n\nDelete helpers are teardown code — they shouldn't fail the test if the\nresource was already removed or modified by the test itself. Asserting\non an ever-growing allowl","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3067],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","hash":"47d3cd26be5cc1729c4e13bc7c2d2db1862266cf","date":"2026-02-17T19:50:10.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Handle app context namespace race during single-spa lifecycle transitions (#1625)","message":"(fix) Handle app context namespace race during single-spa lifecycle transitions (#1625)\n\n* (fix) Handle app context namespace race during single-spa lifecycle transitions\n\nWhen extensions using useDefineAppContext unmount and remount across separate\nsingle-spa lifecycles (e.g., navigating away from the ward page and back), the\nnew instance's effect can fire before the old instance's cleanup has run. This\ncaused registerContext to throw \"Attempted to re-register namespace\" because\nthe namespace was still registered from the stale instance.\n\nThe fix addresses both sides of the race in useDefineAppContext:\n\n- Mount-time: check if the namespace already exists via getContext before\n  attempting registration. If it does, update the existing context instead of\n  calling registerContext (which would throw).\n\n- Cleanup-time: track namespace ownership via a module-level Map of symbol\n  tokens. Each instance claims ownership on mount. The cleanup effect only\n  calls unregisterContext if the current instance is still the owner,\n  preventing a stale cleanup from removing a newer instance's context.\n\nregisterContext in esm-context retains its strict throw for direct callers,\npreserving the uniqueness contract at the API level. The resilience layer\nlives entirely in useDefineAppContext where the lifecycle race originates.\n\nTrade-off: two genuinely different components using the same namespace via\nuseDefineAppContext will no longer hard-fail; the newer one silently wins\nwith a console.error. This is acceptable because (a) the previous behavior\nwas an app crash, (b) the error is logged for debugging, and (c) true\nnamespace collisions are programming errors caught during development.\n\nRef: O3-5434\n\n* (fix) Address review feedback: downgrade console.error to console.warn\n\nThe namespace race condition is an expected scenario during navigation,\nnot an application error. console.warn is more appropriate and avoids\nnoise in error telemetry.\n\n* (fix) Fix SonarQube negated condition warning","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":["O3-5434"],"pullRequests":[1625],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"b63bf8d59ee16c4fdf7dd10f3783c4ac76e31748","date":"2026-02-05T12:19:19.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Render em-dash separators in medication displays conditionally","message":"(fix) Render em-dash separators in medication displays conditionally\n\nEm-dash (—) separators between medication order fields (dose, route,\nfrequency, duration, refills, dosing instructions) were rendered\nunconditionally, causing orphaned leading dashes when preceding fields\nwere absent. This was most visible for free text dosing orders, where\ndose, route, and frequency are all null.\n\nAdditionally, \"Indefinite duration\" was always shown when duration was\nnull, even for free text orders where it adds no useful information\nsince there are no structured dosing fields to contextualize it.\n\nFixes the separator logic in all three medication display components:\n- medication-record (Orders widget)\n- medications-details-table (Active/Past Medications widget)\n- medications-summary (Past Visits widget)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"3e1e88e3371df36f44d36a4872ae3745548a268b","date":"2026-01-12T19:33:11.000Z","author":"Balkawade Sai Dipak","subject":"(test) Add unit tests for ConditionsActionMenu component (#2911)","message":"(test) Add unit tests for ConditionsActionMenu component (#2911)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[2911],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"770e1f73e27c092ed296fcfef9106fc6cd7c0f8f","date":"2026-01-10T12:49:05.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Fix wrong records being shown or modified on paginated tables (#2937)","message":"(fix) Fix wrong records being shown or modified on paginated tables (#2937)\n\nFix critical bugs where interacting with items on page 2+ of paginated\ntables would operate on the wrong record, causing potential data corruption\nand patient safety issues.\n\nAffected components:\n- Programs overview: Action menu edited wrong enrollment; also fixed\n  conditional rendering to show completed programs\n- Programs detailed summary: Improved action menu robustness\n- Immunizations: Expanded row showed wrong vaccine details\n- Encounters: Fixed type error and improved robustness\n\nRoot cause: Components were using array indices from paginated rows to\naccess the source data array, causing index misalignment. Fixed by using\nUUID-based Map lookups for direct access.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[2937],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"f48abd7f30f5a167b6b952ca4f1c8a412bde6167","date":"2025-12-09T23:52:21.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(test) Wait for section title change before expecting end time input in edit visit test","message":"(test) Wait for section title change before expecting end time input in edit visit test\n\nAdds a wait condition for the section title to change to \"Visit start and end date\"\nbefore expecting the end time input to be visible. This ensures the form state has\npropagated through useWatch and the component has re-rendered with visitStatus='past'\nbefore looking for conditionally rendered elements.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"}],"filters":{"repos":["github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-fhir2","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib"],"revisions":["HEAD"],"messageTerms":["condition","visit diagnos","encounter diagnos","RFC"],"count":50},"coverageGaps":[],"truncated":["commits: showing 50 of 115 found","commits: answer byte cap reached; showing 22 of 115 found"]}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8a41210-13c5-40eb-88d8-295f472700ba","uuid":"eba8231d-7615-43d4-a35b-6cf17aa8021c","timestamp":"2026-10-31T15:31:49.923Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"e8bf5eeaa08a65b4b8b1845e4ca1a224f3f90790","date":"2026-09-14T10:31:33.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)","message":"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)\n\n* (fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form\n\nMake condition search results keyboard accessible with visible focus and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep the selected condition name in the input.\n\nUse Record condition for creation and Edit condition for editing. Update translations and cover keyboard navigation and workspace titles in component and browser tests.\n\n* Remove unused conditions workspace title prop\n\nThe conditions form sets its edit title on Workspace2. Remove the unused launch prop and translation dependency, and update the action menu test to match.\n\n* Keep condition search focus when results refresh\n\nReturn focus to the search input when loading removes a focused result. Leave focus alone when the user has moved elsewhere, and test that keyboard input continues in the intended field.","ticketKeys":["O3-5969"],"pullRequests":[3646],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","hash":"6ec18930c2e6e6d7b7ba9062c015114547be9806","date":"2026-09-11T19:55:33.000Z","author":"Ian","subject":"(fix) Move hard lifecycle stop to framework instead of single-spa (#1867)","message":"(fix) Move hard lifecycle stop to framework instead of single-spa (#1867)\n\n* (fix) Move hard lifecycle stop to framework instead of single-spa\n\nsingle-spa's \"timeouts\" actually become `setTimeout()` calls that are\nnot cleared, even when the event they are waiting for has already\nhappened. The upshot of this is that pushing the 15s hard timeout for\nlifecycles to single-spa wound up holding references to unmounted apps\nunconditionally for 15s, even after the actual contents had unmounted.\n\nBy moving the hard timeouts into our framework and reverting to\nsingle-spa's defaults, we greatly reduce the window that single-spa will\nhold the references to its default of 3s. Short of patching single-spa,\nthis seems like the best way we can work around this issue.\n\n* Create changeset\n\n* Address review feedback\n\n* (chore) Add docs\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: openmrs-bot <infrastructure@openmrs.org>","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[1867],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","hash":"818b3b6fe433f1e3da65f25857866fd9308851bb","date":"2026-09-10T18:20:35.000Z","author":"Ian","subject":"(BREAKING) Switch from the style-loader to CSS loader in production mode (#1869)","message":"(BREAKING) Switch from the style-loader to CSS loader in production mode (#1869)\n\n* (feat) Switch from the style-loader to CSS loader in production mode\n\nThis is the implementation of RFC-0033, removing our use of CSS-in-JS\nfrom apps and the framework. In order to keep the output of both rspack\nand webpack in sync, it implements a slightly larger surface than expected,\nbasically ensuring we're using a consistent browserlist.\n\nThis also removes the \"main\" chunk we were generating, but which was\nunreachable, since our entry point was always the module federation\nloader and then the index chunk.\n\nFinally, this adds a rspack / webpack plugin to enforce the rule that an\napp must not change global styles of Carbon components, but may make any\nadjustments provided those are appropriately scoped.\n\n* Add integration test covering CSS assets\n\n* Support data-extension-* as valid targeted selectors\n\n* Address code review comments and align with JS branch\n\n* Up the test timeout for integration tests\n\n* Create changeset\n\n* Fix failing test on CI","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[1869],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"324603e9b2d62756416654585d2e6c1d1653fa14","date":"2026-09-01T20:29:42.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label (#3612)","message":"(fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label (#3612)\n\n* (fix) Label overflow menu triggers via iconDescription instead of aria-label\n\nOn @carbon/react 1.x, the classic OverflowMenu pulls aria-label out of its props and applies it to the menu body (the ul with role menu), not to the trigger button. The trigger's accessible name comes from iconDescription, which defaults to 'Options'. Every overflow menu in this repo passed its label via aria-label, so screen readers announced a generic 'Options' for all of them.\n\nPass the label through iconDescription instead in the visit timeline, encounters table, orders and medications tables, and the allergies, conditions, procedures, programs, and vitals action menus. The conditions menu label was a hardcoded string, so it is now translated. Unit tests and e2e specs that located the triggers by the 'Options' name now use the real labels.\n\n* Keep aria-label on overflow menus so the popup stays named\n\nCarbon's classic OverflowMenu applies aria-label to the opened menu body (the ul with role menu), so dropping it left the popup without an accessible name. Keep aria-label alongside iconDescription so the trigger and the popup are both named. The encounters table test now asserts the popup's aria-label.\n\n* Disambiguate the delete confirmation locators in the e2e specs\n\nThe allergies, biometrics, and vitals trigger names now contain the word delete, so the modal confirmation locator getByRole('button', { name: /delete/i }) matched two elements and failed in strict mode. Target the modal's danger button instead, matching the existing conditions spec.\n\n* Cover the remaining overflow menu labels\n\nName the procedures, attachment preview, and clinical encounter list menus consistently. Remove the misplaced attachment menu item label and cover the accessible names in focused tests.\n\n* Update the procedures and attachments e2e locators for the new trigger names\n\nThe procedures and attachment preview triggers a","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3612],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","hash":"a9fdbfc0f5c2a09368c3fb6e777fc3c274629f76","date":"2026-07-16T13:02:24.000Z","author":"denniskigen","subject":"(fix) Only render diagnosis code span when a code exists","message":"(fix) Only render diagnosis code span when a code exists\n\nFollow-up to #767. Diagnoses without a terminology mapping rendered an\nempty code span with a reserved 4rem column, indenting their labels to\nmatch coded entries. Render the code span conditionally instead so\ncodeless diagnoses display without the placeholder gap.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"64d3c9902168b1a43b08d5da09558e7da6288a0d","date":"2026-06-19T13:21:12.000Z","author":"Nethmi Rodrigo","subject":"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)","message":"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3403],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"bd0350391135e8e0cb8ac61cabd0e3ce5256b28d","date":"2026-06-09T13:10:29.000Z","author":"sfortune","subject":"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)","message":"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)\n\nfix(O3-5709): use table-of-contents icon for Conditions to distinguish from task list\n\nThe Conditions item in the patient chart's left nav and the Task list in\nthe right rail both rendered omrs-icon-list-checked, falsely implying a\nsemantic link between a longitudinal clinical problem list and operational\naction items.\n\nSwitch Conditions to omrs-icon-table-of-contents, an already-registered,\nunclaimed glyph that reads as a list without the checklist connotation. This\nis an interim fix: the durable solution is a dedicated Conditions glyph in\nesm-styleguide (so ConditionsIcon stops aliasing ListCheckedIcon), tracked\nunder O3-5709.\n\nCo-authored-by: denniskigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","ticketKeys":["O3-5709"],"pullRequests":[3359],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","hash":"f36d54777376cc8ce804cc10db6b7ff7da498536","date":"2026-05-29T13:41:24.000Z","author":"denniskigen","subject":"(fix) Add patient procedures app to e2e environment","message":"(fix) Add patient procedures app to e2e environment\n\nThe downstream e2e job (run-e2e-on-other-repos) serves a hardcoded set of\nfrontend modules assembled in run-e2e-docker-env.sh, then runs each\ndownstream repo's specs against it. patient-chart added procedures.spec.ts\n(#3338), which navigates to /chart/procedures and waits for the \"Record\nprocedures\" button rendered by @openmrs/esm-patient-procedures-app.\n\nThat app was missing from the assembled import map, so the dashboard never\nrendered and the spec hit the 180s timeout on every run, including main.\nThe stuck test also held a Playwright worker for the full timeout, which\nintermittently tipped the conditions and vitals form-launch specs over\ntheir own timeouts.\n\nAdd the procedures app so the spec can run. The backend image\n(reference-application-3-backend:nightly-with-data) already carries the\nprocedure concepts, as patient-chart's own e2e passes the full spec.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"3568fa685f2d33a17b6fb975b089ed4b0abb5cfe","date":"2026-05-17T21:37:59.000Z","author":"denniskigen","subject":"fix: prevent escaped condition duplicate warnings","message":"fix: prevent escaped condition duplicate warnings","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"05cfbca7dbdd7488e868e1ffcb5d1ff0a00aac8b","date":"2026-04-30T10:50:10.000Z","author":"Skengmann","subject":"(fix) Correct casing of editCondition label (#3170)","message":"(fix) Correct casing of editCondition label (#3170)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3170],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"c7c10df4f1bec30712d71b2557e3222251827436","date":"2026-04-30T10:04:20.000Z","author":"Devarasetty Praneeth","subject":"(fix) O3-5444: Show inline warning when adding a duplicate condition (#3227)","message":"(fix) O3-5444: Show inline warning when adding a duplicate condition (#3227)","ticketKeys":["O3-5444"],"pullRequests":[3227],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"d92a26c2a1c087c33f22cee56bf2b07c5eb96495","date":"2026-04-22T20:56:54.000Z","author":"omeri innocent","subject":"(fix) O3-5614: Fix delete-condition retry and conditions search input (#3254)","message":"(fix) O3-5614: Fix delete-condition retry and conditions search input (#3254)","ticketKeys":["O3-5614"],"pullRequests":[3254],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"2c514a99a75389e9ccf680a9584eb68db57a2267","date":"2026-04-21T11:18:02.000Z","author":"Om Srivastava","subject":"(fix) O3-5618: Validate condition selection before submit triggers (#3240)","message":"(fix) O3-5618: Validate condition selection before submit triggers (#3240)","ticketKeys":["O3-5618"],"pullRequests":[3240],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"7fa740c199cb105713451efcc641d0a250b0ef59","date":"2026-04-01T21:20:31.000Z","author":"solomonfortune","subject":"(feat) O3-5580: Default clinical status to active when recording a new condition (#3195)","message":"(feat) O3-5580: Default clinical status to active when recording a new condition (#3195)","ticketKeys":["O3-5580"],"pullRequests":[3195],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"7f324ebd5b575f0bbb5868d71a7245c9957eeaba","date":"2026-03-19T13:01:47.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Improve drug order workspace UX (#3138)","message":"(fix) Improve drug order workspace UX (#3138)\n\n- Preserve search term when navigating back from the order form\n- Cancel on new orders returns to drug search instead of closing the workspace\n- Auto-focus the drug search input\n- Hide dose section in order basket tile when dosage is null\n- Fix conditional separators in order basket tile to avoid dangling dashes\n- Allow long drug names to wrap instead of clipping in order basket tiles\n- Remove redundant validation error snackbar from drug order form\n- Remove unused imports and translation keys","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3138],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"b2270525c8afea42e924e28916c44fa398fef91c","date":"2026-03-09T15:30:10.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Treat zero as a valid vitals value instead of falsy/empty (#3084)","message":"(fix) Treat zero as a valid vitals value instead of falsy/empty (#3084)\n\n* (fix) Treat zero as a valid vitals value instead of falsy/empty\n\nJavaScript treats 0 as falsy, which caused zero-valued vitals to be\nsilently skipped across the entire pipeline — fetching, display,\nflagging, validation, and persistence.\n\nReplace all truthiness checks (if (value), Boolean(value), value && ...)\nwith explicit null checks (value != null && value !== '') so that 0 is\ntreated as a real recorded value while undefined, null, and empty strings\ncontinue to mean \"no value\".\n\nAffected layers:\n- assessValue: 0 is now evaluated against reference ranges and flagged\n- prepareObsForSubmission: 0-valued obs are created; editing to 0 no\n  longer voids the old obs without creating a replacement\n- data.resource: 0-valued FHIR observations are no longer dropped from\n  the encounter hash table\n- VitalsHeaderItem: 0 displays with its unit instead of \"Not available\"\n- vitals-header.extension: unit symbols render for 0-valued vitals\n- Form workspace: interpretation and range validation run for 0 values\n- Schema: a form with only a 0-valued field passes \"at least one field\"\n- Input validity: typing 0 is no longer flagged as invalid input\n\n* (fix) Address review feedback: null-check range thresholds and MUAC conditional\n\n- assessValue: use != null for range threshold checks (hiCritical,\n  hiNormal, lowCritical, lowNormal) so a threshold of 0 is not skipped\n- vitals header: use != null for MUAC conditional rendering for\n  consistency with the rest of the patch","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3084],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"ac1012bafec8f832c80d5557bc5e818f8e2143ee","date":"2026-03-04T19:01:35.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Improve E2E test reliability (#3067)","message":"(fix) Improve E2E test reliability (#3067)\n\n* (fix) Improve E2E test reliability\n\nReplace fragile locators and fix test infrastructure issues that cause\nintermittent E2E failures.\n\nSelectors:\n- Replace .nth(0) positional selectors with row-scoped locators\n  (dataRow, getByRole('row').filter()) across allergies, biometrics,\n  conditions, drug-orders, lab-orders, results-viewer, visit-note, and\n  vitals specs\n- Replace CSS class selectors ([class*=\"previewContainer\"]) with\n  role-based locators in attachment preview tests\n- Use getByLabel instead of getByText for form input fields in\n  drug-orders\n- Add role=\"dialog\" and aria-label to attachment preview component\n  for stable test targeting\n\nAssertions:\n- Replace snapshot assertions (textContent + expect) with auto-retrying\n  Playwright assertions (toHaveText, toHaveValue) in edit-existing-visit\n- Wrap bare .isVisible() calls with expect() in immunizations\n- Add missing await on visitsPage.goTo() in results-viewer\n- Remove swallowed .catch(() => {}) on assertion in attachments\n\nTest state:\n- Convert module-level mutable state to per-test fixtures in\n  drug-orders and lab-orders specs (retry/parallel safe)\n- Use test patient fixture instead of manual creation in\n  visit-context-navigation\n- Add try/finally with null guards for cleanup of manually created\n  resources\n\nCleanup helpers:\n- Add response status assertions to deleteEncounter, deleteDrugOrder,\n  deleteTestOrder (accept 200/204/400/404/500)\n- Add ok() assertion to endVisit (accept 200/400 for already-ended\n  visits) and getVisit\n- Remove unnecessary empty request bodies from delete helpers\n\nDrug order recording:\n- Handle environment differences where the order basket may open the\n  drug search workspace directly or require an additional click\n\n* Drop status assertions from delete cleanup helpers\n\nDelete helpers are teardown code — they shouldn't fail the test if the\nresource was already removed or modified by the test itself. Asserting\non an ever-growing allowl","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3067],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","hash":"47d3cd26be5cc1729c4e13bc7c2d2db1862266cf","date":"2026-02-17T19:50:10.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Handle app context namespace race during single-spa lifecycle transitions (#1625)","message":"(fix) Handle app context namespace race during single-spa lifecycle transitions (#1625)\n\n* (fix) Handle app context namespace race during single-spa lifecycle transitions\n\nWhen extensions using useDefineAppContext unmount and remount across separate\nsingle-spa lifecycles (e.g., navigating away from the ward page and back), the\nnew instance's effect can fire before the old instance's cleanup has run. This\ncaused registerContext to throw \"Attempted to re-register namespace\" because\nthe namespace was still registered from the stale instance.\n\nThe fix addresses both sides of the race in useDefineAppContext:\n\n- Mount-time: check if the namespace already exists via getContext before\n  attempting registration. If it does, update the existing context instead of\n  calling registerContext (which would throw).\n\n- Cleanup-time: track namespace ownership via a module-level Map of symbol\n  tokens. Each instance claims ownership on mount. The cleanup effect only\n  calls unregisterContext if the current instance is still the owner,\n  preventing a stale cleanup from removing a newer instance's context.\n\nregisterContext in esm-context retains its strict throw for direct callers,\npreserving the uniqueness contract at the API level. The resilience layer\nlives entirely in useDefineAppContext where the lifecycle race originates.\n\nTrade-off: two genuinely different components using the same namespace via\nuseDefineAppContext will no longer hard-fail; the newer one silently wins\nwith a console.error. This is acceptable because (a) the previous behavior\nwas an app crash, (b) the error is logged for debugging, and (c) true\nnamespace collisions are programming errors caught during development.\n\nRef: O3-5434\n\n* (fix) Address review feedback: downgrade console.error to console.warn\n\nThe namespace race condition is an expected scenario during navigation,\nnot an application error. console.warn is more appropriate and avoids\nnoise in error telemetry.\n\n* (fix) Fix SonarQube negated condition warning","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":["O3-5434"],"pullRequests":[1625],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"b63bf8d59ee16c4fdf7dd10f3783c4ac76e31748","date":"2026-02-05T12:19:19.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Render em-dash separators in medication displays conditionally","message":"(fix) Render em-dash separators in medication displays conditionally\n\nEm-dash (—) separators between medication order fields (dose, route,\nfrequency, duration, refills, dosing instructions) were rendered\nunconditionally, causing orphaned leading dashes when preceding fields\nwere absent. This was most visible for free text dosing orders, where\ndose, route, and frequency are all null.\n\nAdditionally, \"Indefinite duration\" was always shown when duration was\nnull, even for free text orders where it adds no useful information\nsince there are no structured dosing fields to contextualize it.\n\nFixes the separator logic in all three medication display components:\n- medication-record (Orders widget)\n- medications-details-table (Active/Past Medications widget)\n- medications-summary (Past Visits widget)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"3e1e88e3371df36f44d36a4872ae3745548a268b","date":"2026-01-12T19:33:11.000Z","author":"Balkawade Sai Dipak","subject":"(test) Add unit tests for ConditionsActionMenu component (#2911)","message":"(test) Add unit tests for ConditionsActionMenu component (#2911)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[2911],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"770e1f73e27c092ed296fcfef9106fc6cd7c0f8f","date":"2026-01-10T12:49:05.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Fix wrong records being shown or modified on paginated tables (#2937)","message":"(fix) Fix wrong records being shown or modified on paginated tables (#2937)\n\nFix critical bugs where interacting with items on page 2+ of paginated\ntables would operate on the wrong record, causing potential data corruption\nand patient safety issues.\n\nAffected components:\n- Programs overview: Action menu edited wrong enrollment; also fixed\n  conditional rendering to show completed programs\n- Programs detailed summary: Improved action menu robustness\n- Immunizations: Expanded row showed wrong vaccine details\n- Encounters: Fixed type error and improved robustness\n\nRoot cause: Components were using array indices from paginated rows to\naccess the source data array, causing index misalignment. Fixed by using\nUUID-based Map lookups for direct access.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[2937],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"f48abd7f30f5a167b6b952ca4f1c8a412bde6167","date":"2025-12-09T23:52:21.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(test) Wait for section title change before expecting end time input in edit visit test","message":"(test) Wait for section title change before expecting end time input in edit visit test\n\nAdds a wait condition for the section title to change to \"Visit start and end date\"\nbefore expecting the end time input to be visible. This ensures the form state has\npropagated through useWatch and the component has re-rendered with visitStatus='past'\nbefore looking for conditionally rendered elements.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"}],"filters":{"repos":["github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-fhir2","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib"],"revisions":["HEAD"],"messageTerms":["condition","visit diagnos","encounter diagnos","RFC"],"count":50},"coverageGaps":[],"truncated":["commits: showing 50 of 115 found","commits: answer byte cap reached; showing 22 of 115 found"]}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NH2WtjB5DVf2BkmNDpk6C3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
