{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DUCN9neXkERQVGBchEbz8y","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","hash":"fcf1b2562d60389dbf88c5383c2d4237d9d1ff8a","date":"2026-10-05T12:02:05.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-6025: Load z-score tables only when a form needs them (#824)","message":"(fix) O3-6025: Load z-score tables only when a form needs them (#824)\n\n* (fix) Load z-score reference tables only for forms that use them\n\nThe WHO reference tables behind the z-score helpers are about 1.3 MB of JSON, and zscore-service imported all eight of them statically. The form engine app imports registerExpressionHelper from the library's entry at startup, so the tables ended up in its startup chunk, and every form open downloaded and parsed them whether or not the form used a z-score helper.\n\nEach table is a dynamic import now. useProcessorDependencies loads the tables for the z-score helpers a form's schema mentions, alongside the processor's own dependencies, so they're in place before initial values or any expression is evaluated. The helpers stay synchronous, because the expression evaluator doesn't await a helper's result before applying an operator to it. getZRefByGenderAndAge is split into one function per reference, so each helper only reads the tables it needs. If a table fails to load, the form still opens, the error is reported, and the helpers that need it return null.\n\nuseProcessorDependencies also reports loading from the first render. Once a form has opened, its field adapters and concepts are cached, so initial values could otherwise be computed before the dependencies had started loading.\n\nIn esm-form-engine-app the startup chunks go from 1,189 KiB to 382 KiB, or from 301 KiB to 114 KiB gzipped.\n\n* (fix) Wait for form dependencies before evaluating growth rules\n\n* Keep form state when the schema object changes\n\nResetting the form session whenever formJson was a new object wiped\nentered values in the patient chart. esm-form-engine-app passes a new\nschema object on every render, and it re-renders once the form is\nmarked dirty, so the first edit was lost.\n\nDrop the session reset in FormFactoryProvider and stop\nuseProcessorDependencies reloading on a new formJson object. The form\nbuilder already remounts FormEngine when its schema changes, so no\n","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":["O3-6025"],"pullRequests":[824],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"4c50ae55de4b35367c7edb12f1e6b1a7b8388b42","date":"2026-09-30T17:04:59.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Revalidate the visit context in invalidateVisitByUuid (#3720)","message":"(fix) Revalidate the visit context in invalidateVisitByUuid (#3720)\n\n* (fix) Revalidate the visit context in invalidateVisitByUuid\n\ninvalidateVisitByUuid passed a RegExp to SWR's mutate. SWR only treats a\nfunction as a key filter, so it serialized the RegExp as a single literal\nkey that matched no cache entry, and the call did nothing.\n\nStarting or editing a visit, switching the visit context, and restoring a\ndeleted visit all store this helper as the patient chart's\nmutateVisitContext. After any of those, later mutateVisitContext calls\n(order basket, form entry, deleting an encounter, the vitals launcher)\nnever refetched the visit until the page was reloaded. The medications\nand orders tables also call it directly.\n\nUse a key filter function instead, like the other helpers in\nrevalidation-utils.ts, and add a test for it.\n\n* Pass invalidateVisitByUuid as a function in the orders table\n\nOrderBasketItemActions called invalidateVisitByUuid while building its\nworkspace group props instead of wrapping it in a function. That left\nmutateVisitContext undefined for order basket workspaces launched from\nthe orders table. Now that invalidateVisitByUuid actually revalidates,\nit also refetched the visit context every time an order row from that\nvisit rendered.\n\n* Handle orders without a visit and test the order basket refresh\n\nUse optional chaining on the order's encounter visit, like the\nmedications table, so mutateVisitContext doesn't throw for an order whose\nencounter has no visit. Encounter.visit is optional in the framework\ntypes and nullable in openmrs-core.\n\nAdd a test that cancelling an order launches the order basket with a\nmutateVisitContext function, since it was undefined before.\n\n* Skip invalidateVisitByUuid when there's no visit UUID\n\nThe medications and orders tables pass encounter.visit?.uuid, so the\nvisit UUID can be undefined. Reflect that in the type and return early\ninstead of scanning the cache for /visit/undefined.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3720],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","hash":"14197959572c1be0268228ebe25612161a3b6412","date":"2026-09-30T17:02:41.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Clear the shared SWR cache on logout (#1919)","message":"(fix) Clear the shared SWR cache on logout (#1919)\n\n* (fix) Clear the shared SWR cache on logout\n\nLogout called SWR's global `mutate`, which targets SWR's default cache\nrather than the shared cache that `openmrsComponentDecorator` provides to\nO3 apps. Logout navigates to the login page without a reload, so the\nprevious user's cached data survived into the next session in the same\ntab and rendered before revalidating.\n\nRedirectLogout now passes `cache` and `mutate` from `useSWRConfig()` to\n`performLogout`, which clears every cached key by name. Clearing by name\nis needed because a key-filter `mutate(() => true)` skips the\n`useSWRInfinite` and `useSWRSubscription` keys.\n\n* Clear the SWR cache before the early login redirect\n\nlogout() marks the session as logged out before it resolves. That\nre-runs the RedirectLogout effect, which redirects to the login page\nbefore performLogout has cleared the cache. Clear the cache in that\nbranch too, right before redirecting.\n\n* Mark the early cache clear as intentionally unawaited\n\nThe unauthenticated branch starts the SWR cache clear without awaiting\nit, because SWR updates the cache synchronously and the redirect only\nneeds that update. Mark the promise with `void` so it reads as\ndeliberately ignored rather than forgotten.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[1919],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"715ec982cb5008f64cf590e3335001b4de19843e","date":"2026-09-29T19:25:43.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-6004: Make lab result entry safe to retry (#3692)","message":"(fix) O3-6004: Make lab result entry safe to retry (#3692)\n\n* (fix) O3-6004: Make lab result entry safe to retry\n\nSave lab results and discontinue the test order in a single encounter\nrequest, then mark the order as fulfilled. The backend saves inline\norders inside the same transaction as the obs, so a failed discontinue\nno longer leaves the results saved behind it.\n\nPreviously the results, the discontinue and the fulfiller update were\nthree separate requests. If a later one failed, the results were already\nsaved, the order was not COMPLETED, and the form stayed in create mode.\nRetrying posted the obs to the encounter again. If the fulfiller update\nwas the one that failed, every retry added another copy and then failed\non the discontinue, because the backend rejects stopping an order twice.\n\nWhen an order already has saved results but is not COMPLETED, the form\nnow fills in the saved values and saving updates those obs. It then\ndiscontinues the order only if it is still active and marks it as\nfulfilled. A failed save refetches the saved results so the next attempt\nsees them.\n\n* Check for saved results when the user saves\n\nDecide whether to create or update results from a fresh fetch of the\norder's encounter at submit time, instead of the results the form loaded\nearlier. After a failed attempt, the form refetches its results in the\nbackground, and Save is available again before that refetch finishes.\nA quick retry in that window used to take the create path again. If the\nfetch fails, nothing is saved.\n\n* Keep the user's edits when saved results load\n\nOnly fill in saved result values for fields the user hasn't changed.\nAfter a failed save, the form refetches the saved results, and if the\nuser corrected a value while that was in flight, the refetched value\nreplaced their correction.\n\n* test: verify lab result edits are saved after delayed refresh\n\nExtend the delayed-results regression test through Save and close. Check that the corrected value is submitted, the workspa","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":["O3-6004"],"pullRequests":[3692],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","hash":"2f1a67586aa88f6f3b42665335334dc6163bd617","date":"2026-09-29T18:27:00.000Z","author":"Ian","subject":"(feat) Ensure the app shell is preloaded upfront (#1912)","message":"(feat) Ensure the app shell is preloaded upfront (#1912)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[1912],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","hash":"c6b7c76f1b8111720369252f3cc20cf9a9d1e6a0","date":"2026-09-28T21:17:38.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Place the app shell's loading spinner and error page in the body grid's app area (#1904)","message":"(fix) Place the app shell's loading spinner and error page in the body grid's app area (#1904)\n\n* (fix) Place the app shell's loading spinner in the body grid's app area\n\nThe app shell appends its startup spinner to <body>, which is a grid with\nnamed areas for the top nav, left nav, app roots and workspace. The\nspinner had no grid area, so the browser auto-placed it in a new row\nbelow those, in the first column. That column is sized min-content, so it\ngrew to the spinner's width (about 84px) and pushed #omrs-apps-container\nto the right until the spinner was removed. The new row also starts below\nthe fold, so the spinner was never visible.\n\nPlacing the spinner in the appRoots area leaves the column widths alone\nand centers the spinner in the viewport. The spinner is removed right\nafter single-spa starts, before any page mounts into\n#omrs-apps-container, so the two don't overlap.\n\nOn a cold load of /spa/system-administration this removes the two layout\nshifts the spinner caused, one when it's added and one when it's removed.\nCLS goes from 0.113 to 0.003 on localhost, and from 0.291 to 0.164 with\n4x CPU throttling on a 1.6 Mbps, 150 ms RTT connection.\n\n* Add a changeset for the loading spinner grid fix\n\nRecords a patch entry for @openmrs/esm-styleguide describing the spinner\nplacement fix, matching the changeset that other merged PRs in this repo\ninclude.\n\n* Place the fatal error page in the body grid's app area too\n\nThe shell's fatal error page had the same problem as the loading spinner.\nrenderFatalErrorPage() appends it to <body> without a grid area, so the\nbrowser auto-placed it in an extra row below the fold, inside the\nmin-content left nav column, which it then widened to fit its content. On\na real startup failure (the Intl.DurationFormat polyfill chunk failing to\nload), users saw a blank page with only an error toast.\n\nThis adds the error page to the spinner's appRoots rule. min-width: 0\nstops a long error message in the code snippet from stretching the column\np","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[1904],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"47ac43e14be3f538904a7c94e509e65624dae35e","date":"2026-09-28T15:35:43.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Pass a string subtitle to the general order form's error snackbar (#3700)","message":"(fix) Pass a string subtitle to the general order form's error snackbar (#3700)\n\nWhen saving a revised general order failed, the form passed the raw\nOpenmrsFetchError to showSnackbar as the subtitle. React can't render an\nError object as a child, so the snackbar host threw and unmounted, and no\nlater snackbars showed until the page was reloaded.\n\nShow the backend's error message instead, falling back to the error's own\nmessage. This matches how the order basket tile and the lab results form\nin this package read order errors. Adds a test for the failed-save path.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3700],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"52ad5642b88661b759f5e130f12e1d73a7fac66a","date":"2026-09-23T08:32:38.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)","message":"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)\n\n* fix: O3-5990 Remove saved visit-note images safely\n\nConfirm removal of a saved image and void its observation through the obs endpoint. This preserves the encounter and diagnoses when the image is the only observation. Refresh attachment, note, and visit data after removal.\n\nExplain that removal takes effect immediately and discarding note edits will not restore the image. Cover cancel, success, and retry after failure. Verify that a blank note and its diagnosis survive removal of the sole image in the local browser and backend.\n\n* style: Put React first in image removal test imports\n\nMove the React import above the test utilities in the saved-image removal modal test.\n\n* fix: Save visit-note image removals with the form\n\nKeep image removals pending until Save and close, with Undo and Discard restoring the draft. Show a dimmed thumbnail and a separate Undo action for images marked for removal.\n\nRetry failed removals without repeating successful deletions, and avoid rewriting the note when only images change. Keep the visit-context header state stable during form updates.\n\n* fix: Refresh visit-note data once per save attempt\n\nRefresh after the removal batch and note save, including partial failures. Add coverage for saved diagnoses and successful and failed removal batches.\n\nSimplify the image markup, separate the error title from its explanation, and remove redundant footer styles.","ticketKeys":["O3-5990"],"pullRequests":[3684],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"e8bf5eeaa08a65b4b8b1845e4ca1a224f3f90790","date":"2026-09-14T10:31:33.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)","message":"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)\n\n* (fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form\n\nMake condition search results keyboard accessible with visible focus and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep the selected condition name in the input.\n\nUse Record condition for creation and Edit condition for editing. Update translations and cover keyboard navigation and workspace titles in component and browser tests.\n\n* Remove unused conditions workspace title prop\n\nThe conditions form sets its edit title on Workspace2. Remove the unused launch prop and translation dependency, and update the action menu test to match.\n\n* Keep condition search focus when results refresh\n\nReturn focus to the search input when loading removes a focused result. Leave focus alone when the user has moved elsewhere, and test that keyboard input continues in the intended field.","ticketKeys":["O3-5969"],"pullRequests":[3646],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"6961c3d13e74a69bc2ed96dc3fa5aa1cc4d86f25","date":"2026-09-11T21:11:25.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)","message":"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)\n\n* (fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes\n\nMake diagnosis search results keyboard accessible and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep tablet row padding on the result button so its click target and focus outline fill the row.\n\nUse Add visit note and Edit visit note consistently in workspace titles and tablet headings. Update translations and cover the keyboard flow and titles in component and browser tests.\n\n* Update visit context test for the add visit note title\n\nThe siderail opens the note workspace in creation mode. Expect Add visit note so the visit context test matches the renamed workspace title.\n\n* Keep diagnosis search focus when results refresh\n\nReturn focus to the corresponding diagnosis input when loading removes a focused result. Preserve focus when the user moves elsewhere, and cover continued typing in both diagnosis searches and the notes field.\n\n* Reduce spacing below open diagnosis results\n\nUse a smaller bottom margin while diagnosis results are visible. Keep the existing spacing when the list is closed. Verified desktop and tablet layouts and the visit-note E2E workflow.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3645],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","hash":"ad9786412cd423a86c54f889b4e87cf6cf59d61e","date":"2026-09-09T16:53:22.000Z","author":"Ian","subject":"(fix) Reduce re-render churn in FormProcessorFactory (#670)","message":"(fix) Reduce re-render churn in FormProcessorFactory (#670)\n\n* (fix) Re-write some core hooks in the form-processor-factory to reduce churn\n\nIn the FormProcessorFactory, there's serious potential for render\ncascades from the combinations of `useEffect()` and `setState()` that\nthen trigger additional `useEffect()` and `setState()` calls. This\ncommit switches to more aggressively caching some of these key hooks so\nthat there's less potential for these cascade to lead to catastrophic\nreloading issues.\n\n* Reduce churn in processor context\n\nThis is basically done by splitting the processor context into a \"static\"\npart that is derived from the form itself and a \"dynamic\" part that may\nbe updated by components downstream of the FormProcessorFactory. This\nmostly should optimize things so that components that depend on the\nprocessor context should mostly get stable objects, assuming they\ncorrectly use the properties of the processor.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[670],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","hash":"8aa137ceb1785269c8c2636ac225f69dcbda3181","date":"2026-08-04T20:19:08.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config (#1827)","message":"(feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config (#1827)\n\n* (feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config\n\nThis is the pilot migration for @openmrs/eslint-config, the new shared\nflat-config package that centralizes the ESLint rules that have been\ncopy-pasted and drifting across the openmrs-esm-* repositories. Since the\nconfig's base preset was ported from this repo's .eslintrc, esm-core is\nthe natural first adopter.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- Bumped eslint from ^8.55.0 to ^9.13.0 (resolves to 9.39.5) and added\n  @openmrs/eslint-config. Removed the seven ESLint plugin devDependencies\n  the shared config now provides.\n- Replaced .eslintrc and .eslintignore with an eslint.config.mjs that\n  spreads the shared config. Flat config also stops config discovery at\n  the project root, which the old .eslintrc never did (it lacked\n  'root: true' and would cascade into parent directories).\n- Dropped '--ext ts,tsx' from the 28 workspace lint scripts, since the\n  flag was removed in ESLint 9 and flat config makes it unnecessary.\n- Removed 20 stale eslint-disable directives across 15 files. ESLint 9\n  reports unused directives by default, where v8 silently ignored them.\n  Most were artifacts of the typescript-eslint v8 rule renames\n  (ban-types was split, no-var-requires was folded into\n  no-require-imports) that the legacy config never accounted for. These\n  are comment and whitespace-only changes.\n- Updated turbo.json's lint cache input to point at eslint.config.mjs,\n  removed dependabot's now-resolved 'ESLint v9 requires flat config\n  migration' ignores, pointed its linting group at eslint and\n  @openmrs/eslint-config, and refreshed the copilot instructions.\n\nAll 30 workspaces lint green with no errors and no warnings, and a\nroot-level 'eslint --max-warnings 0' run (what lint-staged executes,\nincluding the e2e specs) exits clean, so adopting the shared config\nintroduced no new findings.\n\n* Hash all linted files in turbo's lint task inputs\n\nWith flat config, 'esli","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[1827],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"64d3c9902168b1a43b08d5da09558e7da6288a0d","date":"2026-06-19T13:21:12.000Z","author":"Nethmi Rodrigo","subject":"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)","message":"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3403],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"bd0350391135e8e0cb8ac61cabd0e3ce5256b28d","date":"2026-06-09T13:10:29.000Z","author":"sfortune","subject":"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)","message":"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)\n\nfix(O3-5709): use table-of-contents icon for Conditions to distinguish from task list\n\nThe Conditions item in the patient chart's left nav and the Task list in\nthe right rail both rendered omrs-icon-list-checked, falsely implying a\nsemantic link between a longitudinal clinical problem list and operational\naction items.\n\nSwitch Conditions to omrs-icon-table-of-contents, an already-registered,\nunclaimed glyph that reads as a list without the checklist connotation. This\nis an interim fix: the durable solution is a dedicated Conditions glyph in\nesm-styleguide (so ConditionsIcon stops aliasing ListCheckedIcon), tracked\nunder O3-5709.\n\nCo-authored-by: denniskigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","ticketKeys":["O3-5709"],"pullRequests":[3359],"linksSource":"message, unverified"}],"filters":{"repos":["github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-fhir2","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib"],"revisions":["HEAD"],"messageTerms":["problem list","problem-list","conditions list","reload","refresh"],"count":30},"coverageGaps":[],"truncated":["commits: showing 30 of 39 found","commits: answer byte cap reached; showing 14 of 39 found"]}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8a41210-13c5-40eb-88d8-295f472700ba","uuid":"29fe25cc-59ab-421e-8768-6b41ca596611","timestamp":"2026-10-31T15:31:54.055Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","hash":"fcf1b2562d60389dbf88c5383c2d4237d9d1ff8a","date":"2026-10-05T12:02:05.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-6025: Load z-score tables only when a form needs them (#824)","message":"(fix) O3-6025: Load z-score tables only when a form needs them (#824)\n\n* (fix) Load z-score reference tables only for forms that use them\n\nThe WHO reference tables behind the z-score helpers are about 1.3 MB of JSON, and zscore-service imported all eight of them statically. The form engine app imports registerExpressionHelper from the library's entry at startup, so the tables ended up in its startup chunk, and every form open downloaded and parsed them whether or not the form used a z-score helper.\n\nEach table is a dynamic import now. useProcessorDependencies loads the tables for the z-score helpers a form's schema mentions, alongside the processor's own dependencies, so they're in place before initial values or any expression is evaluated. The helpers stay synchronous, because the expression evaluator doesn't await a helper's result before applying an operator to it. getZRefByGenderAndAge is split into one function per reference, so each helper only reads the tables it needs. If a table fails to load, the form still opens, the error is reported, and the helpers that need it return null.\n\nuseProcessorDependencies also reports loading from the first render. Once a form has opened, its field adapters and concepts are cached, so initial values could otherwise be computed before the dependencies had started loading.\n\nIn esm-form-engine-app the startup chunks go from 1,189 KiB to 382 KiB, or from 301 KiB to 114 KiB gzipped.\n\n* (fix) Wait for form dependencies before evaluating growth rules\n\n* Keep form state when the schema object changes\n\nResetting the form session whenever formJson was a new object wiped\nentered values in the patient chart. esm-form-engine-app passes a new\nschema object on every render, and it re-renders once the form is\nmarked dirty, so the first edit was lost.\n\nDrop the session reset in FormFactoryProvider and stop\nuseProcessorDependencies reloading on a new formJson object. The form\nbuilder already remounts FormEngine when its schema changes, so no\n","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":["O3-6025"],"pullRequests":[824],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"4c50ae55de4b35367c7edb12f1e6b1a7b8388b42","date":"2026-09-30T17:04:59.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Revalidate the visit context in invalidateVisitByUuid (#3720)","message":"(fix) Revalidate the visit context in invalidateVisitByUuid (#3720)\n\n* (fix) Revalidate the visit context in invalidateVisitByUuid\n\ninvalidateVisitByUuid passed a RegExp to SWR's mutate. SWR only treats a\nfunction as a key filter, so it serialized the RegExp as a single literal\nkey that matched no cache entry, and the call did nothing.\n\nStarting or editing a visit, switching the visit context, and restoring a\ndeleted visit all store this helper as the patient chart's\nmutateVisitContext. After any of those, later mutateVisitContext calls\n(order basket, form entry, deleting an encounter, the vitals launcher)\nnever refetched the visit until the page was reloaded. The medications\nand orders tables also call it directly.\n\nUse a key filter function instead, like the other helpers in\nrevalidation-utils.ts, and add a test for it.\n\n* Pass invalidateVisitByUuid as a function in the orders table\n\nOrderBasketItemActions called invalidateVisitByUuid while building its\nworkspace group props instead of wrapping it in a function. That left\nmutateVisitContext undefined for order basket workspaces launched from\nthe orders table. Now that invalidateVisitByUuid actually revalidates,\nit also refetched the visit context every time an order row from that\nvisit rendered.\n\n* Handle orders without a visit and test the order basket refresh\n\nUse optional chaining on the order's encounter visit, like the\nmedications table, so mutateVisitContext doesn't throw for an order whose\nencounter has no visit. Encounter.visit is optional in the framework\ntypes and nullable in openmrs-core.\n\nAdd a test that cancelling an order launches the order basket with a\nmutateVisitContext function, since it was undefined before.\n\n* Skip invalidateVisitByUuid when there's no visit UUID\n\nThe medications and orders tables pass encounter.visit?.uuid, so the\nvisit UUID can be undefined. Reflect that in the type and return early\ninstead of scanning the cache for /visit/undefined.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3720],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","hash":"14197959572c1be0268228ebe25612161a3b6412","date":"2026-09-30T17:02:41.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Clear the shared SWR cache on logout (#1919)","message":"(fix) Clear the shared SWR cache on logout (#1919)\n\n* (fix) Clear the shared SWR cache on logout\n\nLogout called SWR's global `mutate`, which targets SWR's default cache\nrather than the shared cache that `openmrsComponentDecorator` provides to\nO3 apps. Logout navigates to the login page without a reload, so the\nprevious user's cached data survived into the next session in the same\ntab and rendered before revalidating.\n\nRedirectLogout now passes `cache` and `mutate` from `useSWRConfig()` to\n`performLogout`, which clears every cached key by name. Clearing by name\nis needed because a key-filter `mutate(() => true)` skips the\n`useSWRInfinite` and `useSWRSubscription` keys.\n\n* Clear the SWR cache before the early login redirect\n\nlogout() marks the session as logged out before it resolves. That\nre-runs the RedirectLogout effect, which redirects to the login page\nbefore performLogout has cleared the cache. Clear the cache in that\nbranch too, right before redirecting.\n\n* Mark the early cache clear as intentionally unawaited\n\nThe unauthenticated branch starts the SWR cache clear without awaiting\nit, because SWR updates the cache synchronously and the redirect only\nneeds that update. Mark the promise with `void` so it reads as\ndeliberately ignored rather than forgotten.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[1919],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"715ec982cb5008f64cf590e3335001b4de19843e","date":"2026-09-29T19:25:43.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-6004: Make lab result entry safe to retry (#3692)","message":"(fix) O3-6004: Make lab result entry safe to retry (#3692)\n\n* (fix) O3-6004: Make lab result entry safe to retry\n\nSave lab results and discontinue the test order in a single encounter\nrequest, then mark the order as fulfilled. The backend saves inline\norders inside the same transaction as the obs, so a failed discontinue\nno longer leaves the results saved behind it.\n\nPreviously the results, the discontinue and the fulfiller update were\nthree separate requests. If a later one failed, the results were already\nsaved, the order was not COMPLETED, and the form stayed in create mode.\nRetrying posted the obs to the encounter again. If the fulfiller update\nwas the one that failed, every retry added another copy and then failed\non the discontinue, because the backend rejects stopping an order twice.\n\nWhen an order already has saved results but is not COMPLETED, the form\nnow fills in the saved values and saving updates those obs. It then\ndiscontinues the order only if it is still active and marks it as\nfulfilled. A failed save refetches the saved results so the next attempt\nsees them.\n\n* Check for saved results when the user saves\n\nDecide whether to create or update results from a fresh fetch of the\norder's encounter at submit time, instead of the results the form loaded\nearlier. After a failed attempt, the form refetches its results in the\nbackground, and Save is available again before that refetch finishes.\nA quick retry in that window used to take the create path again. If the\nfetch fails, nothing is saved.\n\n* Keep the user's edits when saved results load\n\nOnly fill in saved result values for fields the user hasn't changed.\nAfter a failed save, the form refetches the saved results, and if the\nuser corrected a value while that was in flight, the refetched value\nreplaced their correction.\n\n* test: verify lab result edits are saved after delayed refresh\n\nExtend the delayed-results regression test through Save and close. Check that the corrected value is submitted, the workspa","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":["O3-6004"],"pullRequests":[3692],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","hash":"2f1a67586aa88f6f3b42665335334dc6163bd617","date":"2026-09-29T18:27:00.000Z","author":"Ian","subject":"(feat) Ensure the app shell is preloaded upfront (#1912)","message":"(feat) Ensure the app shell is preloaded upfront (#1912)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[1912],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","hash":"c6b7c76f1b8111720369252f3cc20cf9a9d1e6a0","date":"2026-09-28T21:17:38.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Place the app shell's loading spinner and error page in the body grid's app area (#1904)","message":"(fix) Place the app shell's loading spinner and error page in the body grid's app area (#1904)\n\n* (fix) Place the app shell's loading spinner in the body grid's app area\n\nThe app shell appends its startup spinner to <body>, which is a grid with\nnamed areas for the top nav, left nav, app roots and workspace. The\nspinner had no grid area, so the browser auto-placed it in a new row\nbelow those, in the first column. That column is sized min-content, so it\ngrew to the spinner's width (about 84px) and pushed #omrs-apps-container\nto the right until the spinner was removed. The new row also starts below\nthe fold, so the spinner was never visible.\n\nPlacing the spinner in the appRoots area leaves the column widths alone\nand centers the spinner in the viewport. The spinner is removed right\nafter single-spa starts, before any page mounts into\n#omrs-apps-container, so the two don't overlap.\n\nOn a cold load of /spa/system-administration this removes the two layout\nshifts the spinner caused, one when it's added and one when it's removed.\nCLS goes from 0.113 to 0.003 on localhost, and from 0.291 to 0.164 with\n4x CPU throttling on a 1.6 Mbps, 150 ms RTT connection.\n\n* Add a changeset for the loading spinner grid fix\n\nRecords a patch entry for @openmrs/esm-styleguide describing the spinner\nplacement fix, matching the changeset that other merged PRs in this repo\ninclude.\n\n* Place the fatal error page in the body grid's app area too\n\nThe shell's fatal error page had the same problem as the loading spinner.\nrenderFatalErrorPage() appends it to <body> without a grid area, so the\nbrowser auto-placed it in an extra row below the fold, inside the\nmin-content left nav column, which it then widened to fit its content. On\na real startup failure (the Intl.DurationFormat polyfill chunk failing to\nload), users saw a blank page with only an error toast.\n\nThis adds the error page to the spinner's appRoots rule. min-width: 0\nstops a long error message in the code snippet from stretching the column\np","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[1904],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"47ac43e14be3f538904a7c94e509e65624dae35e","date":"2026-09-28T15:35:43.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Pass a string subtitle to the general order form's error snackbar (#3700)","message":"(fix) Pass a string subtitle to the general order form's error snackbar (#3700)\n\nWhen saving a revised general order failed, the form passed the raw\nOpenmrsFetchError to showSnackbar as the subtitle. React can't render an\nError object as a child, so the snackbar host threw and unmounted, and no\nlater snackbars showed until the page was reloaded.\n\nShow the backend's error message instead, falling back to the error's own\nmessage. This matches how the order basket tile and the lab results form\nin this package read order errors. Adds a test for the failed-save path.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3700],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"52ad5642b88661b759f5e130f12e1d73a7fac66a","date":"2026-09-23T08:32:38.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)","message":"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)\n\n* fix: O3-5990 Remove saved visit-note images safely\n\nConfirm removal of a saved image and void its observation through the obs endpoint. This preserves the encounter and diagnoses when the image is the only observation. Refresh attachment, note, and visit data after removal.\n\nExplain that removal takes effect immediately and discarding note edits will not restore the image. Cover cancel, success, and retry after failure. Verify that a blank note and its diagnosis survive removal of the sole image in the local browser and backend.\n\n* style: Put React first in image removal test imports\n\nMove the React import above the test utilities in the saved-image removal modal test.\n\n* fix: Save visit-note image removals with the form\n\nKeep image removals pending until Save and close, with Undo and Discard restoring the draft. Show a dimmed thumbnail and a separate Undo action for images marked for removal.\n\nRetry failed removals without repeating successful deletions, and avoid rewriting the note when only images change. Keep the visit-context header state stable during form updates.\n\n* fix: Refresh visit-note data once per save attempt\n\nRefresh after the removal batch and note save, including partial failures. Add coverage for saved diagnoses and successful and failed removal batches.\n\nSimplify the image markup, separate the error title from its explanation, and remove redundant footer styles.","ticketKeys":["O3-5990"],"pullRequests":[3684],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"e8bf5eeaa08a65b4b8b1845e4ca1a224f3f90790","date":"2026-09-14T10:31:33.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)","message":"(fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form (#3646)\n\n* (fix) O3-5969: Improve keyboard access and edit wording in the conditions form\n\nMake condition search results keyboard accessible with visible focus and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep the selected condition name in the input.\n\nUse Record condition for creation and Edit condition for editing. Update translations and cover keyboard navigation and workspace titles in component and browser tests.\n\n* Remove unused conditions workspace title prop\n\nThe conditions form sets its edit title on Workspace2. Remove the unused launch prop and translation dependency, and update the action menu test to match.\n\n* Keep condition search focus when results refresh\n\nReturn focus to the search input when loading removes a focused result. Leave focus alone when the user has moved elsewhere, and test that keyboard input continues in the intended field.","ticketKeys":["O3-5969"],"pullRequests":[3646],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"6961c3d13e74a69bc2ed96dc3fa5aa1cc4d86f25","date":"2026-09-11T21:11:25.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)","message":"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)\n\n* (fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes\n\nMake diagnosis search results keyboard accessible and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep tablet row padding on the result button so its click target and focus outline fill the row.\n\nUse Add visit note and Edit visit note consistently in workspace titles and tablet headings. Update translations and cover the keyboard flow and titles in component and browser tests.\n\n* Update visit context test for the add visit note title\n\nThe siderail opens the note workspace in creation mode. Expect Add visit note so the visit context test matches the renamed workspace title.\n\n* Keep diagnosis search focus when results refresh\n\nReturn focus to the corresponding diagnosis input when loading removes a focused result. Preserve focus when the user moves elsewhere, and cover continued typing in both diagnosis searches and the notes field.\n\n* Reduce spacing below open diagnosis results\n\nUse a smaller bottom margin while diagnosis results are visible. Keep the existing spacing when the list is closed. Verified desktop and tablet layouts and the visit-note E2E workflow.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3645],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","hash":"ad9786412cd423a86c54f889b4e87cf6cf59d61e","date":"2026-09-09T16:53:22.000Z","author":"Ian","subject":"(fix) Reduce re-render churn in FormProcessorFactory (#670)","message":"(fix) Reduce re-render churn in FormProcessorFactory (#670)\n\n* (fix) Re-write some core hooks in the form-processor-factory to reduce churn\n\nIn the FormProcessorFactory, there's serious potential for render\ncascades from the combinations of `useEffect()` and `setState()` that\nthen trigger additional `useEffect()` and `setState()` calls. This\ncommit switches to more aggressively caching some of these key hooks so\nthat there's less potential for these cascade to lead to catastrophic\nreloading issues.\n\n* Reduce churn in processor context\n\nThis is basically done by splitting the processor context into a \"static\"\npart that is derived from the form itself and a \"dynamic\" part that may\nbe updated by components downstream of the FormProcessorFactory. This\nmostly should optimize things so that components that depend on the\nprocessor context should mostly get stable objects, assuming they\ncorrectly use the properties of the processor.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[670],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","hash":"8aa137ceb1785269c8c2636ac225f69dcbda3181","date":"2026-08-04T20:19:08.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config (#1827)","message":"(feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config (#1827)\n\n* (feat) Adopt ESLint 9 and the shared @openmrs/eslint-config\n\nThis is the pilot migration for @openmrs/eslint-config, the new shared\nflat-config package that centralizes the ESLint rules that have been\ncopy-pasted and drifting across the openmrs-esm-* repositories. Since the\nconfig's base preset was ported from this repo's .eslintrc, esm-core is\nthe natural first adopter.\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- Bumped eslint from ^8.55.0 to ^9.13.0 (resolves to 9.39.5) and added\n  @openmrs/eslint-config. Removed the seven ESLint plugin devDependencies\n  the shared config now provides.\n- Replaced .eslintrc and .eslintignore with an eslint.config.mjs that\n  spreads the shared config. Flat config also stops config discovery at\n  the project root, which the old .eslintrc never did (it lacked\n  'root: true' and would cascade into parent directories).\n- Dropped '--ext ts,tsx' from the 28 workspace lint scripts, since the\n  flag was removed in ESLint 9 and flat config makes it unnecessary.\n- Removed 20 stale eslint-disable directives across 15 files. ESLint 9\n  reports unused directives by default, where v8 silently ignored them.\n  Most were artifacts of the typescript-eslint v8 rule renames\n  (ban-types was split, no-var-requires was folded into\n  no-require-imports) that the legacy config never accounted for. These\n  are comment and whitespace-only changes.\n- Updated turbo.json's lint cache input to point at eslint.config.mjs,\n  removed dependabot's now-resolved 'ESLint v9 requires flat config\n  migration' ignores, pointed its linting group at eslint and\n  @openmrs/eslint-config, and refreshed the copilot instructions.\n\nAll 30 workspaces lint green with no errors and no warnings, and a\nroot-level 'eslint --max-warnings 0' run (what lint-staged executes,\nincluding the e2e specs) exits clean, so adopting the shared config\nintroduced no new findings.\n\n* Hash all linted files in turbo's lint task inputs\n\nWith flat config, 'esli","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[1827],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"64d3c9902168b1a43b08d5da09558e7da6288a0d","date":"2026-06-19T13:21:12.000Z","author":"Nethmi Rodrigo","subject":"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)","message":"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3403],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"bd0350391135e8e0cb8ac61cabd0e3ce5256b28d","date":"2026-06-09T13:10:29.000Z","author":"sfortune","subject":"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)","message":"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)\n\nfix(O3-5709): use table-of-contents icon for Conditions to distinguish from task list\n\nThe Conditions item in the patient chart's left nav and the Task list in\nthe right rail both rendered omrs-icon-list-checked, falsely implying a\nsemantic link between a longitudinal clinical problem list and operational\naction items.\n\nSwitch Conditions to omrs-icon-table-of-contents, an already-registered,\nunclaimed glyph that reads as a list without the checklist connotation. This\nis an interim fix: the durable solution is a dedicated Conditions glyph in\nesm-styleguide (so ConditionsIcon stops aliasing ListCheckedIcon), tracked\nunder O3-5709.\n\nCo-authored-by: denniskigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","ticketKeys":["O3-5709"],"pullRequests":[3359],"linksSource":"message, unverified"}],"filters":{"repos":["github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-core","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-fhir2","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib"],"revisions":["HEAD"],"messageTerms":["problem list","problem-l