{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014V6UWH1ewkUVtVo9Ura4WW","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"d0f4b1bf5be04ad6f9c567635864b36de6ac36c3","date":"2026-10-07T13:20:03.000Z","author":"Veronica Mukuhi Muthee","subject":"(feat) O3-5823: Capture diagnosis rank and certainty in the visit note (#3621)","message":"(feat) O3-5823: Capture diagnosis rank and certainty in the visit note (#3621)","ticketKeys":["O3-5823"],"pullRequests":[3621],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","hash":"0e1edc234479890d45bc09e67b2ee25befc1c803","date":"2026-10-05T11:52:41.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-6027: Clear order and diagnosis submissions on every write (#826)","message":"(fix) O3-6027: Clear order and diagnosis submissions on every write (#826)\n\n* (fix) Clear order and diagnosis submissions on every write\n\nOrdersAdapter and EncounterDiagnosisAdapter now clear the field's\nsubmission at the start of transformFieldValue, the same way ObsAdapter\nalready does.\n\ngracefullySetSubmission only sets values and never clears them, so a\nnewValue from an earlier write stayed on the field after it was\ncleared. On a new encounter, selecting an order or diagnosis and then\nclearing the field still submitted it. On an edited encounter, swapping\na stored order or diagnosis for another value and then clearing the\nfield still submitted the swapped value: a NEW order alongside the\nvoid, or an edit of the stored diagnosis to the swapped concept.\nClearing first means nothing is submitted for a new encounter and only\nthe void goes out for an edited one.\n\neditOrder no longer needs its own clearSubmission call when the value\nmatches the stored order, since the submission is already empty.\n\n* Fixup","ticketKeys":["O3-6027"],"pullRequests":[826],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","hash":"ebb02b719931d121419669b531b6e05c77f515e9","date":"2026-10-02T18:57:25.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-6030: Keep hidden obs group members, orders and diagnoses out of submissions (#822)","message":"(fix) O3-6030: Keep hidden obs group members, orders and diagnoses out of submissions (#822)\n\n* (fix) Keep hidden obs group members, orders and diagnoses out of submissions\n\nHide logic only kept hidden top-level obs out of the encounter payload.\nHidden obs group members, test orders and diagnoses kept whatever value\nwas entered before the field was hidden, so they were still submitted\neven though the form no longer showed them.\n\nprocessObsGroup now skips hidden members and, in edit mode, voids their\nstored obs, the same way top-level obs are handled. It reads each\nmember's visibility and stored obs from the flattened form field,\nbecause hide evaluation and hydration update that copy rather than the\none held in the group's questions. prepareOrders and prepareDiagnosis\nnow skip hidden fields.\n\n* Evaluate hide logic for repeated field instances\n\nRows added to a repeating field kept their hidden state from when they\nwere created, so hiding a repeating test order, diagnosis or obs group\nmember left its extra rows in the encounter payload. Extra group rows\nalso stayed visible in the form.\n\nfindFieldSection looks up the field's page through meta.pageId, which\nrepeated instances don't carry because cloneRepeatField replaces their\nmeta. Reading sections off the missing page threw inside the\nfieldDependents loop in handleFieldLogic, so none of the repeated\ninstances had their hide expression re-evaluated. It now returns\nundefined when the page isn't found, which skips the section visibility\nupdate for repeated instances since they aren't in the form schema.\n\n* (fix) Preserve pending deletions for hidden orders and diagnoses\n\nFiltering hidden fields out of encounter submissions discarded explicit deletions when a previously cleared field became hidden. Keep pending voided values for hidden orders and diagnoses while excluding their new values. Leave stored values untouched when no deletion is pending, and preserve existing submission behavior for visible fields.\n\n* Skip delete","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":["O3-6030"],"pullRequests":[822],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"4d9f19a2d629347559fe32b89899af6245c16e23","date":"2026-09-24T15:31:10.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5989: Keep a visit note saved when one of its images is rejected (#3670)","message":"(fix) O3-5989: Keep a visit note saved when one of its images is rejected (#3670)\n\nBy the time the images upload, the note and its diagnoses are already on\nthe server. A rejected image used to bubble into the catch handler, which\nshowed \"Error saving visit note\" and left the form open in create mode, so\nthe next Save and close posted a second note.\n\nUploads now run with Promise.allSettled. Every image the server accepts is\nsaved, the workspace closes as usual, and a warning snackbar names the\nimages that were rejected with the server's reason, pointing the user at\nthe note to add them again. A failure to save the note itself still shows\nthe error and keeps the form open.","ticketKeys":["O3-5989"],"pullRequests":[3670],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"52ad5642b88661b759f5e130f12e1d73a7fac66a","date":"2026-09-23T08:32:38.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)","message":"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)\n\n* fix: O3-5990 Remove saved visit-note images safely\n\nConfirm removal of a saved image and void its observation through the obs endpoint. This preserves the encounter and diagnoses when the image is the only observation. Refresh attachment, note, and visit data after removal.\n\nExplain that removal takes effect immediately and discarding note edits will not restore the image. Cover cancel, success, and retry after failure. Verify that a blank note and its diagnosis survive removal of the sole image in the local browser and backend.\n\n* style: Put React first in image removal test imports\n\nMove the React import above the test utilities in the saved-image removal modal test.\n\n* fix: Save visit-note image removals with the form\n\nKeep image removals pending until Save and close, with Undo and Discard restoring the draft. Show a dimmed thumbnail and a separate Undo action for images marked for removal.\n\nRetry failed removals without repeating successful deletions, and avoid rewriting the note when only images change. Keep the visit-context header state stable during form updates.\n\n* fix: Refresh visit-note data once per save attempt\n\nRefresh after the removal batch and note save, including partial failures. Add coverage for saved diagnoses and successful and failed removal batches.\n\nSimplify the image markup, separate the error title from its explanation, and remove redundant footer styles.","ticketKeys":["O3-5990"],"pullRequests":[3684],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"6961c3d13e74a69bc2ed96dc3fa5aa1cc4d86f25","date":"2026-09-11T21:11:25.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)","message":"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)\n\n* (fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes\n\nMake diagnosis search results keyboard accessible and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep tablet row padding on the result button so its click target and focus outline fill the row.\n\nUse Add visit note and Edit visit note consistently in workspace titles and tablet headings. Update translations and cover the keyboard flow and titles in component and browser tests.\n\n* Update visit context test for the add visit note title\n\nThe siderail opens the note workspace in creation mode. Expect Add visit note so the visit context test matches the renamed workspace title.\n\n* Keep diagnosis search focus when results refresh\n\nReturn focus to the corresponding diagnosis input when loading removes a focused result. Preserve focus when the user moves elsewhere, and cover continued typing in both diagnosis searches and the notes field.\n\n* Reduce spacing below open diagnosis results\n\nUse a smaller bottom margin while diagnosis results are visible. Keep the existing spacing when the list is closed. Verified desktop and tablet layouts and the visit-note E2E workflow.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3645],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"1a2af778aa7f86ea2c1fc944e46d6a7548af2f88","date":"2026-07-21T19:50:58.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5822: Dedupe diagnoses in visit-level rollups (#3496)","message":"(fix) O3-5822: Dedupe diagnoses in visit-level rollups (#3496)","ticketKeys":["O3-5822"],"pullRequests":[3496],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"23534665aa959b2921f11401aa2e275db61501f7","date":"2026-07-17T10:38:00.000Z","author":"denniskigen","subject":"(chore) Include ngx-formentry in the OpenMRS dependency auto-update","message":"(chore) Include ngx-formentry in the OpenMRS dependency auto-update\n\nThe 4-hourly updater covers the framework, the React form engine lib,\nand the openmrs tooling, but not the Angular form engine, so the\nesm-form-entry-app lockfile resolution for @openmrs/ngx-formentry@next\nfroze at 20.0.1-pre.525 while the engine kept moving (the current next\nis pre.564, carrying the ICD-11 diagnosis code display, the endpoint\ndata source, and the remote-select centering fixes). Adding the package\nto the yarn up list lets the existing automation open the catch-up PR\nand keep the Angular engine current alongside its React peer.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"e9b29360b21e0e0db589259b64f1ea4840f7f542","date":"2026-07-17T07:21:41.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(feat) O3-5815: Return ICD-11 codes for diagnoses in the form-entry datasources (#3479)","message":"(feat) O3-5815: Return ICD-11 codes for diagnoses in the form-entry datasources (#3479)\n\nThe Angular form engine passes a diagnosis question's schema-level\ndatasource config (datasource.config, including conceptSourceUuid) to\nsearchOptions and resolveSelectedValue. The diagnoses datasource\npreviously ignored it, so no terminology code could be displayed next\nto a diagnosis.\n\n- findDiagnoses and resolveConcept accept an optional dataSourceOptions\n  argument. When it names a conceptSourceUuid, the concept search and\n  the selected-value lookup request conceptMappings in the rep and emit\n  a code field on the option, so the picker can render\n  \"{ICD11CODE} {Name}\" per the KNHTS convention.\n- The code comes from the concept's mapping to the configured source,\n  preferring SAME-AS mappings over other map types.\n- Concepts without a mapping to the source, and questions without the\n  config, behave exactly as before. Other datasources that share\n  mapConcept and resolveConcept are unchanged.\n\nCompanion to openmrs/openmrs-ngx-formentry#176, which renders the code\nfield.","ticketKeys":["O3-5815"],"pullRequests":[3479],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","hash":"a9fdbfc0f5c2a09368c3fb6e777fc3c274629f76","date":"2026-07-16T13:02:24.000Z","author":"denniskigen","subject":"(fix) Only render diagnosis code span when a code exists","message":"(fix) Only render diagnosis code span when a code exists\n\nFollow-up to #767. Diagnoses without a terminology mapping rendered an\nempty code span with a reserved 4rem column, indenting their labels to\nmatch coded entries. Render the code span conditionally instead so\ncodeless diagnoses display without the placeholder gap.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","hash":"208fcc7720fc4f0ca48efb721cf74e7850af2a32","date":"2026-07-16T07:03:19.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(feat) O3-5815: Show ICD-11 codes next to diagnoses (#767)","message":"(feat) O3-5815: Show ICD-11 codes next to diagnoses (#767)","ticketKeys":["O3-5815"],"pullRequests":[767],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"64d3c9902168b1a43b08d5da09558e7da6288a0d","date":"2026-06-19T13:21:12.000Z","author":"Nethmi Rodrigo","subject":"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)","message":"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3403],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","hash":"2204ac05b44795dec06b132c0d15ca1b010bcd95","date":"2026-05-13T13:35:49.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(chore) Migrate from jest to vitest (#742)","message":"(chore) Migrate from jest to vitest (#742)\n\n* (chore) Migrate from jest to vitest\n\nSwap the test runner from jest to vitest, aligning form-engine-lib\nwith the patterns adopted across the rest of the O3 apps.\n\n- Replace jest, @swc/jest, jest-cli, jest-environment-jsdom, and\n  @types/jest with vitest, @vitest/coverage-v8, jsdom, and cross-env.\n  Bump @testing-library/dom (9.x to 10.x), @testing-library/jest-dom\n  (6.4 to 6.8), and @testing-library/react (14.x to 16.x) so the\n  /vitest subpath is available. Keep jest-when on jest-when@^3.x: its\n  fluent API works against vitest's vi.fn() unchanged because vitest\n  mocks are jest-API-compatible.\n- Add vitest.config.ts: jsdom environment, .scss/.css aliased to\n  identity-obj-proxy via the anchored ^.*\\.s?css$ regex,\n  @openmrs/esm-framework aliased to its mock, react-i18next and\n  react-markdown aliased to their local __mocks__ files,\n  __mocks__/* and src/* aliased so the bare imports the jest\n  config used to resolve via moduleDirectories continue to work,\n  and fakeTimers.toFake limited so it does not break React's\n  scheduler.\n- Replace src/setup-tests.ts's '@testing-library/jest-dom' import\n  with '@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest', drop the 'jest-when'\n  side-effect import (no longer needed), swap jest.fn for vi.fn in\n  the i18next mock, and convert the require('resize-observer-polyfill')\n  call to a proper ESM import.\n- Rewrite __mocks__/react-i18next.js's I18nextProvider entry to a\n  plain function component, since the previous jest.fn() call only\n  worked under jest's globals.\n- Convert the 41 test files to the vitest API: explicit imports for\n  describe/expect/it/test/vi (plus beforeEach/afterEach/type Mock\n  where used), jest.* swapped for vi.*. The many vi.mock(path, ...\n  jest.requireActual(path), override) factories rewritten as the\n  async vi.mock(path, async () => ({ ...((await vi.importActual(path))\n  as object), override })) form. The vi.mock(name, () => vi.fn())\n  factory wrapped in { default: vi.fn() ","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[742],"linksSource":"message, unverified"}],"filters":{"repos":["github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-fhir2","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-emrapi"],"revisions":["HEAD"],"messageTerms":["encounter-diagnosis","encounter diagnosis","diagnos","category"],"after":"2026-04-01","count":40},"coverageGaps":[],"truncated":[]}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8a41210-13c5-40eb-88d8-295f472700ba","uuid":"cf3f202a-f499-4f7d-ade6-bcd382167a44","timestamp":"2026-10-31T15:32:14.735Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"d0f4b1bf5be04ad6f9c567635864b36de6ac36c3","date":"2026-10-07T13:20:03.000Z","author":"Veronica Mukuhi Muthee","subject":"(feat) O3-5823: Capture diagnosis rank and certainty in the visit note (#3621)","message":"(feat) O3-5823: Capture diagnosis rank and certainty in the visit note (#3621)","ticketKeys":["O3-5823"],"pullRequests":[3621],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","hash":"0e1edc234479890d45bc09e67b2ee25befc1c803","date":"2026-10-05T11:52:41.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-6027: Clear order and diagnosis submissions on every write (#826)","message":"(fix) O3-6027: Clear order and diagnosis submissions on every write (#826)\n\n* (fix) Clear order and diagnosis submissions on every write\n\nOrdersAdapter and EncounterDiagnosisAdapter now clear the field's\nsubmission at the start of transformFieldValue, the same way ObsAdapter\nalready does.\n\ngracefullySetSubmission only sets values and never clears them, so a\nnewValue from an earlier write stayed on the field after it was\ncleared. On a new encounter, selecting an order or diagnosis and then\nclearing the field still submitted it. On an edited encounter, swapping\na stored order or diagnosis for another value and then clearing the\nfield still submitted the swapped value: a NEW order alongside the\nvoid, or an edit of the stored diagnosis to the swapped concept.\nClearing first means nothing is submitted for a new encounter and only\nthe void goes out for an edited one.\n\neditOrder no longer needs its own clearSubmission call when the value\nmatches the stored order, since the submission is already empty.\n\n* Fixup","ticketKeys":["O3-6027"],"pullRequests":[826],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","hash":"ebb02b719931d121419669b531b6e05c77f515e9","date":"2026-10-02T18:57:25.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-6030: Keep hidden obs group members, orders and diagnoses out of submissions (#822)","message":"(fix) O3-6030: Keep hidden obs group members, orders and diagnoses out of submissions (#822)\n\n* (fix) Keep hidden obs group members, orders and diagnoses out of submissions\n\nHide logic only kept hidden top-level obs out of the encounter payload.\nHidden obs group members, test orders and diagnoses kept whatever value\nwas entered before the field was hidden, so they were still submitted\neven though the form no longer showed them.\n\nprocessObsGroup now skips hidden members and, in edit mode, voids their\nstored obs, the same way top-level obs are handled. It reads each\nmember's visibility and stored obs from the flattened form field,\nbecause hide evaluation and hydration update that copy rather than the\none held in the group's questions. prepareOrders and prepareDiagnosis\nnow skip hidden fields.\n\n* Evaluate hide logic for repeated field instances\n\nRows added to a repeating field kept their hidden state from when they\nwere created, so hiding a repeating test order, diagnosis or obs group\nmember left its extra rows in the encounter payload. Extra group rows\nalso stayed visible in the form.\n\nfindFieldSection looks up the field's page through meta.pageId, which\nrepeated instances don't carry because cloneRepeatField replaces their\nmeta. Reading sections off the missing page threw inside the\nfieldDependents loop in handleFieldLogic, so none of the repeated\ninstances had their hide expression re-evaluated. It now returns\nundefined when the page isn't found, which skips the section visibility\nupdate for repeated instances since they aren't in the form schema.\n\n* (fix) Preserve pending deletions for hidden orders and diagnoses\n\nFiltering hidden fields out of encounter submissions discarded explicit deletions when a previously cleared field became hidden. Keep pending voided values for hidden orders and diagnoses while excluding their new values. Leave stored values untouched when no deletion is pending, and preserve existing submission behavior for visible fields.\n\n* Skip delete","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":["O3-6030"],"pullRequests":[822],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"4d9f19a2d629347559fe32b89899af6245c16e23","date":"2026-09-24T15:31:10.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5989: Keep a visit note saved when one of its images is rejected (#3670)","message":"(fix) O3-5989: Keep a visit note saved when one of its images is rejected (#3670)\n\nBy the time the images upload, the note and its diagnoses are already on\nthe server. A rejected image used to bubble into the catch handler, which\nshowed \"Error saving visit note\" and left the form open in create mode, so\nthe next Save and close posted a second note.\n\nUploads now run with Promise.allSettled. Every image the server accepts is\nsaved, the workspace closes as usual, and a warning snackbar names the\nimages that were rejected with the server's reason, pointing the user at\nthe note to add them again. A failure to save the note itself still shows\nthe error and keeps the form open.","ticketKeys":["O3-5989"],"pullRequests":[3670],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"52ad5642b88661b759f5e130f12e1d73a7fac66a","date":"2026-09-23T08:32:38.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)","message":"(fix) O3-5990: Remove saved visit-note images safely (#3684)\n\n* fix: O3-5990 Remove saved visit-note images safely\n\nConfirm removal of a saved image and void its observation through the obs endpoint. This preserves the encounter and diagnoses when the image is the only observation. Refresh attachment, note, and visit data after removal.\n\nExplain that removal takes effect immediately and discarding note edits will not restore the image. Cover cancel, success, and retry after failure. Verify that a blank note and its diagnosis survive removal of the sole image in the local browser and backend.\n\n* style: Put React first in image removal test imports\n\nMove the React import above the test utilities in the saved-image removal modal test.\n\n* fix: Save visit-note image removals with the form\n\nKeep image removals pending until Save and close, with Undo and Discard restoring the draft. Show a dimmed thumbnail and a separate Undo action for images marked for removal.\n\nRetry failed removals without repeating successful deletions, and avoid rewriting the note when only images change. Keep the visit-context header state stable during form updates.\n\n* fix: Refresh visit-note data once per save attempt\n\nRefresh after the removal batch and note save, including partial failures. Add coverage for saved diagnoses and successful and failed removal batches.\n\nSimplify the image markup, separate the error title from its explanation, and remove redundant footer styles.","ticketKeys":["O3-5990"],"pullRequests":[3684],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"6961c3d13e74a69bc2ed96dc3fa5aa1cc4d86f25","date":"2026-09-11T21:11:25.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)","message":"(fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes (#3645)\n\n* (fix) Improve keyboard access and add/edit titles in visit notes\n\nMake diagnosis search results keyboard accessible and return focus to the search input after selection. Keep tablet row padding on the result button so its click target and focus outline fill the row.\n\nUse Add visit note and Edit visit note consistently in workspace titles and tablet headings. Update translations and cover the keyboard flow and titles in component and browser tests.\n\n* Update visit context test for the add visit note title\n\nThe siderail opens the note workspace in creation mode. Expect Add visit note so the visit context test matches the renamed workspace title.\n\n* Keep diagnosis search focus when results refresh\n\nReturn focus to the corresponding diagnosis input when loading removes a focused result. Preserve focus when the user moves elsewhere, and cover continued typing in both diagnosis searches and the notes field.\n\n* Reduce spacing below open diagnosis results\n\nUse a smaller bottom margin while diagnosis results are visible. Keep the existing spacing when the list is closed. Verified desktop and tablet layouts and the visit-note E2E workflow.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3645],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"1a2af778aa7f86ea2c1fc944e46d6a7548af2f88","date":"2026-07-21T19:50:58.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5822: Dedupe diagnoses in visit-level rollups (#3496)","message":"(fix) O3-5822: Dedupe diagnoses in visit-level rollups (#3496)","ticketKeys":["O3-5822"],"pullRequests":[3496],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"23534665aa959b2921f11401aa2e275db61501f7","date":"2026-07-17T10:38:00.000Z","author":"denniskigen","subject":"(chore) Include ngx-formentry in the OpenMRS dependency auto-update","message":"(chore) Include ngx-formentry in the OpenMRS dependency auto-update\n\nThe 4-hourly updater covers the framework, the React form engine lib,\nand the openmrs tooling, but not the Angular form engine, so the\nesm-form-entry-app lockfile resolution for @openmrs/ngx-formentry@next\nfroze at 20.0.1-pre.525 while the engine kept moving (the current next\nis pre.564, carrying the ICD-11 diagnosis code display, the endpoint\ndata source, and the remote-select centering fixes). Adding the package\nto the yarn up list l