{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BSmp1Ptbozy7X7vGNdNHpK","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"1a2af778aa7f86ea2c1fc944e46d6a7548af2f88","date":"2026-07-21T19:50:58.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5822: Dedupe diagnoses in visit-level rollups (#3496)","message":"(fix) O3-5822: Dedupe diagnoses in visit-level rollups (#3496)","ticketKeys":["O3-5822"],"pullRequests":[3496],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"23534665aa959b2921f11401aa2e275db61501f7","date":"2026-07-17T10:38:00.000Z","author":"denniskigen","subject":"(chore) Include ngx-formentry in the OpenMRS dependency auto-update","message":"(chore) Include ngx-formentry in the OpenMRS dependency auto-update\n\nThe 4-hourly updater covers the framework, the React form engine lib,\nand the openmrs tooling, but not the Angular form engine, so the\nesm-form-entry-app lockfile resolution for @openmrs/ngx-formentry@next\nfroze at 20.0.1-pre.525 while the engine kept moving (the current next\nis pre.564, carrying the ICD-11 diagnosis code display, the endpoint\ndata source, and the remote-select centering fixes). Adding the package\nto the yarn up list lets the existing automation open the catch-up PR\nand keep the Angular engine current alongside its React peer.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"e9b29360b21e0e0db589259b64f1ea4840f7f542","date":"2026-07-17T07:21:41.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(feat) O3-5815: Return ICD-11 codes for diagnoses in the form-entry datasources (#3479)","message":"(feat) O3-5815: Return ICD-11 codes for diagnoses in the form-entry datasources (#3479)\n\nThe Angular form engine passes a diagnosis question's schema-level\ndatasource config (datasource.config, including conceptSourceUuid) to\nsearchOptions and resolveSelectedValue. The diagnoses datasource\npreviously ignored it, so no terminology code could be displayed next\nto a diagnosis.\n\n- findDiagnoses and resolveConcept accept an optional dataSourceOptions\n  argument. When it names a conceptSourceUuid, the concept search and\n  the selected-value lookup request conceptMappings in the rep and emit\n  a code field on the option, so the picker can render\n  \"{ICD11CODE} {Name}\" per the KNHTS convention.\n- The code comes from the concept's mapping to the configured source,\n  preferring SAME-AS mappings over other map types.\n- Concepts without a mapping to the source, and questions without the\n  config, behave exactly as before. Other datasources that share\n  mapConcept and resolveConcept are unchanged.\n\nCompanion to openmrs/openmrs-ngx-formentry#176, which renders the code\nfield.","ticketKeys":["O3-5815"],"pullRequests":[3479],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","hash":"a9fdbfc0f5c2a09368c3fb6e777fc3c274629f76","date":"2026-07-16T13:02:24.000Z","author":"denniskigen","subject":"(fix) Only render diagnosis code span when a code exists","message":"(fix) Only render diagnosis code span when a code exists\n\nFollow-up to #767. Diagnoses without a terminology mapping rendered an\nempty code span with a reserved 4rem column, indenting their labels to\nmatch coded entries. Render the code span conditionally instead so\ncodeless diagnoses display without the placeholder gap.","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","hash":"208fcc7720fc4f0ca48efb721cf74e7850af2a32","date":"2026-07-16T07:03:19.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(feat) O3-5815: Show ICD-11 codes next to diagnoses (#767)","message":"(feat) O3-5815: Show ICD-11 codes next to diagnoses (#767)","ticketKeys":["O3-5815"],"pullRequests":[767],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"b147fb5906f1c3df18f12e3c804daeea486813d2","date":"2026-06-22T11:11:48.000Z","author":"Nethmi Rodrigo","subject":"(fix) Attach visit to visit note submissions (#3406)","message":"(fix) Attach visit to visit note submissions (#3406)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3406],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"64d3c9902168b1a43b08d5da09558e7da6288a0d","date":"2026-06-19T13:21:12.000Z","author":"Nethmi Rodrigo","subject":"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)","message":"(fix) Filter conditions query to problem-list-item category (#3403)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3403],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"6c28b2d62b57153a8a829e3507fea1c91cd54584","date":"2026-06-16T18:15:25.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(test) Add e2e coverage for deleting program enrollments and editing visit notes (#3388)","message":"(test) Add e2e coverage for deleting program enrollments and editing visit notes (#3388)","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[3388],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"bd0350391135e8e0cb8ac61cabd0e3ce5256b28d","date":"2026-06-09T13:10:29.000Z","author":"sfortune","subject":"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)","message":"(fix) O3-5709: Change the conditions left-nav icon to distinguish it from the task list (#3359)\n\nfix(O3-5709): use table-of-contents icon for Conditions to distinguish from task list\n\nThe Conditions item in the patient chart's left nav and the Task list in\nthe right rail both rendered omrs-icon-list-checked, falsely implying a\nsemantic link between a longitudinal clinical problem list and operational\naction items.\n\nSwitch Conditions to omrs-icon-table-of-contents, an already-registered,\nunclaimed glyph that reads as a list without the checklist connotation. This\nis an interim fix: the durable solution is a dedicated Conditions glyph in\nesm-styleguide (so ConditionsIcon stops aliasing ListCheckedIcon), tracked\nunder O3-5709.\n\nCo-authored-by: denniskigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","ticketKeys":["O3-5709"],"pullRequests":[3359],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"3568fa685f2d33a17b6fb975b089ed4b0abb5cfe","date":"2026-05-17T21:37:59.000Z","author":"denniskigen","subject":"fix: prevent escaped condition duplicate warnings","message":"fix: prevent escaped condition duplicate warnings","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[],"linksSource":"message, unverified"},{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib","hash":"2204ac05b44795dec06b132c0d15ca1b010bcd95","date":"2026-05-13T13:35:49.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(chore) Migrate from jest to vitest (#742)","message":"(chore) Migrate from jest to vitest (#742)\n\n* (chore) Migrate from jest to vitest\n\nSwap the test runner from jest to vitest, aligning form-engine-lib\nwith the patterns adopted across the rest of the O3 apps.\n\n- Replace jest, @swc/jest, jest-cli, jest-environment-jsdom, and\n  @types/jest with vitest, @vitest/coverage-v8, jsdom, and cross-env.\n  Bump @testing-library/dom (9.x to 10.x), @testing-library/jest-dom\n  (6.4 to 6.8), and @testing-library/react (14.x to 16.x) so the\n  /vitest subpath is available. Keep jest-when on jest-when@^3.x: its\n  fluent API works against vitest's vi.fn() unchanged because vitest\n  mocks are jest-API-compatible.\n- Add vitest.config.ts: jsdom environment, .scss/.css aliased to\n  identity-obj-proxy via the anchored ^.*\\.s?css$ regex,\n  @openmrs/esm-framework aliased to its mock, react-i18next and\n  react-markdown aliased to their local __mocks__ files,\n  __mocks__/* and src/* aliased so the bare imports the jest\n  config used to resolve via moduleDirectories continue to work,\n  and fakeTimers.toFake limited so it does not break React's\n  scheduler.\n- Replace src/setup-tests.ts's '@testing-library/jest-dom' import\n  with '@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest', drop the 'jest-when'\n  side-effect import (no longer needed), swap jest.fn for vi.fn in\n  the i18next mock, and convert the require('resize-observer-polyfill')\n  call to a proper ESM import.\n- Rewrite __mocks__/react-i18next.js's I18nextProvider entry to a\n  plain function component, since the previous jest.fn() call only\n  worked under jest's globals.\n- Convert the 41 test files to the vitest API: explicit imports for\n  describe/expect/it/test/vi (plus beforeEach/afterEach/type Mock\n  where used), jest.* swapped for vi.*. The many vi.mock(path, ...\n  jest.requireActual(path), override) factories rewritten as the\n  async vi.mock(path, async () => ({ ...((await vi.importActual(path))\n  as object), override })) form. The vi.mock(name, () => vi.fn())\n  factory wrapped in { default: vi.fn() ","messageCut":"message cut to 2000 characters","ticketKeys":[],"pullRequests":[742],"linksSource":"message, unverified"}],"filters":{"repos":["github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-module-fhir2","github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-form-engine-lib"],"revisions":["HEAD"],"messageTerms":["conditions","condition","diagnos","visit note"],"after":"2026-05-01","before":"2026-07-31","count":40},"coverageGaps":[],"truncated":[]}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8a41210-13c5-40eb-88d8-295f472700ba","uuid":"19ae1741-8e74-4e7a-836a-43809f84d339","timestamp":"2026-10-31T15:32:23.192Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-chart","hash":"1a2af778aa7f86ea2c1fc944e46d6a7548af2f88","date":"2026-07-21T19:50:58.000Z","author":"Dennis Kigen","subject":"(fix) O3-5822: Dedupe diagnoses in visit-level rollups (#3496)","message":"(fix) O3-5822: Dedupe diagnoses in visit-level rollups (#3496)